{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release: build design for slice 1 (the exporter and the checked package)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: revision 6, for council round 74f. No code yet.** Release work was opened by the council under D439 (D758). The behaviour is\n     4\tfixed by D726, D756 and `FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4). This page holds the AGENTS §2 tables for the first slice.\n     5\t\n     6\t**Revision 2 answers `codex-r74.md`** (see `claude-r74.md`):\n     7\t- the pass condition is an origin check of every field against its stored source, not a string sweep;\n     8\t- a missing source item is refused;\n     9\t- the package is checked before it is moved into place;\n    10\t- the manifest is a closed set;\n    11\t- the bound is validated as a date;\n    12\t- narrow reads;\n    13\t- size and speed budgets;\n    14\t- tests that separate every branch;\n    15\t- `object`, `kind` and groups dropped;\n    16\t- no idea submission.\n    17\t\n    18\tThe evidence summary stays as extraction stored it (§8, disputed in `claude-r74.md`).\n    19\t\n    20\t**Revision 3 answers `codex-r74b.md`.**\n    21\t- The checker derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package: the date, each question's class, the records and their counts.\n    22\t- A missing source item refuses `check` too.\n    23\t- The files must be two regular, non-symlink files, with no duplicate JSON member names.\n    24\t- The staging folder has one owner.\n    25\t- The builder's refusal is tested through the builder.\n    26\t- The diagnostics read only the columns a store has.\n    27\t\n    28\t**Revision 4 answers `codex-r74c.md`.**\n    29\t- One date rule for build and `check`.\n    30\t- Questions are ordered by `created_seq, rowid`.\n    31\t- (Superseded in revision 5.) The build claimed its output folder before staging.\n    32\t- Cleanup sits where the staging path is known.\n    33\t- A report failure after publication has its own outcome.\n    34\t- The builder's refusal is proved through the real command on a scratch copy.\n    35\t- Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 are sharpened.\n    36\t\n    37\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r74d.md` with one structural rule** (AGENTS §1: the publication mechanism drew findings in 74b, 74c and\n    38\t74d). Staging is private, and the only public step is one atomic move that refuses any existing destination. There is no public\n    39\tclaim, so nothing public is created early or cleaned up. Staging is removed in a `finally` covering its whole life, so any error,\n    40\tdatabase errors included, leaves nothing at `--out`.\n    41\t\n    42\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r74e.md`.**\n    43\t- The build's cleanup responsibility ends the moment `publish` succeeds: the staging path is cleared and the `finally` removes nothing\n    44\t  after that, so a folder later created at the freed staging name is never touched.\n    45\t- The late refusal at `publish`, and the end of cleanup after it, are proved through the real command on scratch copies with a\n    46\t  pause.\n    47\t\n    48\t## 0. Scope\n    49\t\n    50\t- **Slice 1 (this page), $0:**\n    51\t  - the exporter `release_export` and its self-check;\n    52\t  - the package writer, the package check and the origin check;\n    53\t  - the release builder, which calls the exporter directly;\n    54\t  - tests and mutants;\n    55\t  - the $0 release check on stored stores.\n    56\t- **Slice 2, next.** The release page reads only the package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite\n    57\t  trials, no idea submission control or route. It gets a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen, which completes D756's screen check.\n    58\t- **No idea submission in the release** (council 74). The idea path (`idea.py`) reads the ledger at every step and calls a paid model\n    59\t  per idea. The design's §5 idea acceptance (an idea card backed only by `v8`, and its composed request) is carried forward as pending\n    60\t  for the first idea-enabled slice.\n    61\t- **Not in scope:**\n    62\t  - the POC, its API, MCP and page (unchanged);\n    63\t  - colleagues' page;\n    64\t  - frozen pieces, extraction included;\n    65\t  - any model call;\n    66\t  - commit, publish, deploy.\n    67\t\n    68\t## 1. What is built\n    69\t\n    70\t`src/hivemind/release.py` is the one owner, beside `service.py`.\n    71\t\n    72\t- **Constants:**\n    73\t  - `FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'`;\n    74\t  - `ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'`;\n    75\t  - `FORECAST_UNAVAILABLE = 'Forecast unavailable'`;\n    76\t  - `PACKAGE_FILES = {'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'}`.\n    77\t- **`ALLOWED`:** the closed key set per record type.\n    78\t\n    79\t  | Record | Keys |\n    80\t  |---|---|\n    81\t  | envelope | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `questions` |\n    82\t  | number question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (= `number`), `forecast` (= the marker), `evidence` |\n    83\t  | event or Yes/No question | `id`, `question`, `open`, `class` (`event` or `yes_no`), `answers` (the two stored rung labels, in position order), `answer` (the stored label of the latest judgement's rung on or before the bound, or null), `evidence` |\n    84\t  | evidence in force at the bound | `id`, `one_line`, `quote`, `tier`, `speaker`, `original_who`, `original_day`, `sources` |\n    85\t  | source recorded on or before the bound | `title`, `publisher`, `day`, `uri` |\n    86\t  | manifest | `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`, `data_sha256` |\n    87\t\n    88\t- **`question_class(views_db, view_id, labels)`** (design §3):\n    89\t  - `event` when the view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES`. The key is read as `select measure from view_keys`, and\n    90\t    only when the table exists;\n    91\t  - `yes_no` when there are exactly two labels which, through `vocabulary.canonical('label', …)`, are `Yes` and `No` in either order;\n    92\t  - `number` otherwise: a view with no key, or one whose bands cannot be resolved.\n    93\t- **`release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None)`:**\n    94\t  - pins both connections (`bundle.read_snapshot`);\n    95\t  - resolves the bound with `service.resolve_bound`, refuses a store with no default day, and validates the bound with\n    96\t    `date.fromisoformat`;\n    97\t  - exports every view that exists at the bound (`service.view_exists`), closed ones included, in `created_seq, rowid` order;\n    98\t  - builds each record field by field from the table above, with column-limited SQL:\n    99\t    - `select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid`;\n   100\t    - `select position, label from rungs`;\n   101\t    - `select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1`;\n   102\t    - `service.is_open_as_of`, which reads only `open` and `after_seq`;\n   103\t  - takes evidence in force from `service.evidence` and its fields from that record;\n   104\t  - looks up each source's `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri` in the items database by `input_id`. A visible source whose item is\n   105\t    missing raises `ReleaseRefused` (there is no fallback to the id);\n   106\t  - calls `check_export` on its own result before returning (AGENTS §3: the writer refuses).\n   107\t- **`check_export(data)`:** the closed-set check.\n   108\t  - Every dict at every level has exactly its record type's keys.\n   109\t  - Value checks:\n   110\t    - `format` and `allow_list` equal the constants, and `as_of` is an ISO date;\n   111\t    - `class` is in its set;\n   112\t    - a number record's `forecast` is the marker;\n   113\t    - `answers` is two strings, and `answer` is one of them or null;\n   114\t    - `open` is a bool and every text field is a string.\n   115\t  - It returns the counts it judged: questions per class, evidence, sources.\n   116\t- **`check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of)`:** the pass condition. It is independent of the exporter's code path.\n   117\t  It derives everything it compares from the store, never from the package.\n   118\t  - **The bound: one rule for both commands.** `expected_as_of` is given by the caller.\n   119\t    - The builder passes the bound it resolved: `service.resolve_bound` on the requested day, or the default when none is given; an\n   120\t      omitted day with no default is refused.\n   121\t    - `check` passes the package's `as_of` through the same `service.resolve_bound`, which refuses a day after a store's last\n   122\t      completed day. A legacy ledger with no completed days accepts any valid date in both commands alike.\n   123\t    - The package's `as_of` must equal `expected_as_of`.\n   124\t  - **The class** of each question is derived from the stored measure and labels (`question_class`). The permitted keys and values\n   125\t    are then chosen from that class, never from the package's `class` field.\n   126\t  - **Order and counts.** The questions are compared as an ordered list in `created_seq, rowid` order, as `bundle.library` orders\n   127\t    them (`old-2/v2` and `v3` share sequence 8). Each question's evidence is compared in link order (`evidence_links.id`), and its\n   128\t    sources in row order (`evidence_sources.id`). A duplicate question, evidence record or source therefore fails.\n   129\t\n   130\t  It compares every field with its permitted stored source at the bound, by direct SQL:\n   131\t  - the question set equals the views visible at the bound, with `question` equal to `views.question`;\n   132\t  - `open` equals the latest visible switch's `open`;\n   133\t  - for `event` and `yes_no`: `answers` equal the rung labels in position order, and `answer` equals the label of the latest judgement\n   134\t    rung on or before the bound, or null;\n   135\t  - for `number`: only the marker;\n   136\t  - the evidence id set equals the links visible at the bound, minus those whose latest replacement is visible, computed in its own\n   137\t    SQL. Each evidence field equals the `evidence` row's column;\n   138\t  - each source list starts from every visible `evidence_sources` row, in row order, with `day` taken from\n   139\t    `evidence_sources.publication_day`. Each row needs a matching `items` row for `title`, `publisher` and `source_uri`; a row with no\n   140\t    item raises `ReleaseRefused` (a left join, so a missing item is never silently dropped).\n   141\t\n   142\t  Any difference raises `ReleaseRefused`, naming the question, the field and the evidence id. It returns the number of fields\n   143\t  compared.\n   144\t- **`stage(out_dir)`:** creates a private staging folder with a name unique to this invocation, `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=out_dir.parent,\n   145\t  prefix='.<name>.staging-')`. Creation is exclusive, so only this invocation owns it. It returns the path.\n   146\t- **`write_package(data, staged)`:** writes `release-data.json` and `manifest.json` into the staging folder. It creates nothing\n   147\t  else.\n   148\t- **`publish(staged, out_dir)`:** one atomic move that refuses any existing destination, empty or not:\n   149\t  - on macOS, `renamex_np(staged, out_dir, RENAME_EXCL)` through `ctypes`. Verified on this Mac: onto a free path it succeeds; onto\n   150\t    an existing empty or non-empty folder it fails with `EEXIST`, and both folders stay as they were;\n   151\t  - on Linux, `renameat2(AT_FDCWD, staged, AT_FDCWD, out_dir, RENAME_NOREPLACE)`;\n   152\t  - where neither call exists, or the filesystem lacks support (`ENOTSUP`, `EINVAL`), it raises `ReleaseRefused`.\n   153\t\n   154\t  It never replaces, creates or removes anything at `out_dir` except by that one move.\n   155\t- **`check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None)`:**\n   156\t  - the directory holds exactly `PACKAGE_FILES`, each a regular file and not a symbolic link (`os.lstat`), with no subdirectories;\n   157\t  - both files parse as JSON with no duplicate member name at any level (an `object_pairs_hook` that refuses a repeated key);\n   158\t  - the manifest has exactly its four keys, and its `format`, `allow_list` and `as_of` equal the data's;\n   159\t  - its sha256 equals the data file's;\n   160\t  - the data passes `check_export`, and, when the stores are given, `check_origins` with the expected bound;\n   161\t  - it returns the counts.\n   162\t- **`withheld_unresolved(views_db, data)`** is for the report only. It lists the number questions whose `service.ladder_bands(rungs)`\n   163\t  returns `(None, reason)`, with the reason and whether the view has a key. Its output never enters the package.\n   164\t\n   165\t`scripts/release_build.py`:\n   166\t- **`build --ledger --items [--as-of] --out`:**\n   167\t  1. refuse an existing `--out` early, as a convenience; `publish` holds the guarantee;\n   168\t  2. resolve the bound once (`service.resolve_bound`, `date.fromisoformat`);\n   169\t  3. `stage(--out)`. From here a `finally` removes this staging folder while the build still owns it;\n   170\t  4. `release_export` at that bound;\n   171\t  5. `write_package` into the staging folder;\n   172\t  6. `check_package` on the staged folder, with the stores and the resolved bound;\n   173\t  7. `publish` to `--out`. The moment it succeeds, the build drops its staging path (`staged = None`); the `finally` then removes\n   174\t     nothing;\n   175\t  8. write `<out>.report.json` beside the package, through a temporary file and `os.replace`.\n   176\t\n   177\t  The failure outcomes:\n   178\t  - **Before publication** (steps 2–7): any exception, whether `ReleaseRefused`, `OSError`, `sqlite3.Error` or another, prints the\n   179\t    reason and exits 1. The `finally` removes this build's staging folder; nothing exists at `--out` from this build. A corrected\n   180\t    retry at the same `--out` succeeds.\n   181\t  - **After publication** (step 8 fails): the package is final and checked. Exit 2 with \"package published and checked; report not\n   182\t    written; run `check` to regenerate it\".\n   183\t\n   184\t  It has no input path for prepared or translated JSON, and it takes no clock reading; the folder name is the caller's (D12, D13).\n   185\t- **`check <out> --ledger --items`:** re-runs `check_package` on an existing package, with the stores, the package's `as_of`\n   186\t  validated against the store (above), and the regular-file and duplicate-key checks. It leaves the package in place and rewrites\n   187\t  `<out>.report.json`. This is also the retry after a report write failed. Its report gives `check_seconds` and marks\n   188\t  `export_seconds` as not measured.\n   189\t- **The report:**\n   190\t  - the store path and the bound;\n   191\t  - counts per class;\n   192\t  - the unresolved list;\n   193\t  - the fields compared;\n   194\t  - bytes;\n   195\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\n   196\t\n   197\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\n   198\t\n   199\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\n   200\t|---|---|---|---|\n   201\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\n   202\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \"no default day; supply --as-of\" | nothing | none |\n   203\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\n   204\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\n   205\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\n   206\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\n   207\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\n   208\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\n   209\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\n   210\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\n   211\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\n   212\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\n   213\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\n   214\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\n   215\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\n   216\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\n   217\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\n   218\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\n   219\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\n   220\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\n   221\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\n   222\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\n   223\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\n   224\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\n   225\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\n   226\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\n   227\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\n   228\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\n   229\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\n   230\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\n   231\t\n   232\t## 3. Value × reader\n   233\t\n   234\tReaders of the package:\n   235\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\n   236\t- the release page (slice 2);\n   237\t- the tests.\n   238\t\n   239\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\n   240\t\n   241\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\n   242\t|---|---|---|\n   243\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\n   244\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\n   245\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\n   246\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\n   247\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\n   248\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\n   249\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\n   250\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\n   251\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\n   252\t\n   253\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\n   254\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\n   255\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\n   256\t- `view_switches.reason`;\n   257\t- `clean_ladders`;\n   258\t- `thesis_groups`;\n   259\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\n   260\t\n   261\t## 4. New path × old checks\n   262\t\n   263\t| Check on the old path (`bundle.library`, `view_bundle`, `service`) | New path |\n   264\t|---|---|\n   265\t| `resolve_bound`: unfinished first day, future bound | same call |\n   266\t| `bundle.library`: no default day refused; `date.fromisoformat` | same two checks |\n   267\t| A view not visible at the bound is not served | same `view_exists` |\n   268\t| Sources visible at the bound; replacements applied | same `service.evidence`, verified independently by `check_origins` |\n   269\t| Pinned read transaction | same `bundle.read_snapshot` |\n   270\t| `item_lookup` falls back to the id for a missing item | refused instead |\n   271\t| A malformed `clean_ladders` row is refused | not read |\n   272\t| Corrupt judgement JSON is refused | no JSON column read |\n   273\t| The UI contract rejects unknown fields | the release's own `check_export`; the page's reading of it is slice 2 |\n   274\t\n   275\t## 5. Prior decisions\n   276\t\n   277\t- D726: number questions show sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with band, forecast text and history withheld together.\n   278\t- D756: Alex's choice.\n   279\t- D757: the design, revision 4.\n   280\t- D758: the release is opened; §4 (a); order.\n   281\t- D12/D13: no clock.\n   282\t- D163: English product text.\n   283\t- D690: poc-v118 stays the product.\n   284\t- D261: the ruler is untouched.\n   285\t- D274: the extraction prompt is frozen.\n   286\t\n   287\t## 6. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\n   288\t\n   289\tThe fixtures use a real store on a temporary path (`store.create_view`, `store.insert`), with a real items database. Each test names\n   290\tits row above:\n   291\t1. **Closed set (§1).**\n   292\t   - Every dict in a fixture export has exactly its type's keys.\n   293\t   - Positive control: an export with one added key fails `check_export`.\n   294\t2. **Number with `lo`/`hi`.** The record carries the marker. No rung label, condition, `reasons`, `why_changed` or `implied_outcome` of\n   295\t   that view appears in any decoded package field.\n   296\t3. **Branch fixtures for identity and the report:**\n   297\t   - a condition-only number that resolves: `number`, and absent from `withheld_unresolved`;\n   298\t   - an unresolved number with a key: `number`, and present;\n   299\t   - an unresolved number without a key: `number`, and present.\n   300\t4. **Yes/No with numeric bounds** (`growth_rate` key, labels Yes/No): `yes_no`, with its answer label. A `why_changed` quoting\n   301\t   \"$1 trillion\" is absent.\n   302\t5. **Event with the served ledger's `v49` labels,** \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\": `event`, with its label kept. A\n   303\t   `why_changed` quoting another question's band is absent.\n   304\t6. **Legacy store** with no `view_keys` table and `是`/`否` labels: `yes_no`.\n   305\t7. **Closing switch** whose reason names the band label: `open: false`, and the reason is absent.\n   306\t8. **Replacement and source visibility** at two bounds. A visible source with a missing item is refused.\n   307\t9. **Package:**\n   308\t   - staged, then checked, passes;\n   309\t   - a foreign file fails, and so does a subdirectory;\n   310\t   - a changed data byte fails;\n   311\t   - an extra manifest key with an unchanged data hash fails;\n   312\t   - a manifest `as_of` differing from the data's fails;\n   313\t   - an existing `--out`, empty or not, is refused, and a leftover staging folder from another build does not block a build.\n   314\t10. **Origin check, each from the store:**\n   315\t    - in a staged copy, the system's forecast text placed in an evidence `one_line` fails, naming the field;\n   316\t    - a Yes/No record turned into a number record, keeping the closed set, fails;\n   317\t    - a duplicated question, and a duplicated evidence record, each fails;\n   318\t    - a package whose `as_of` is a day later than the store's last completed day fails `check`;\n   319\t    - a legacy fixture with no completed days, built at an explicit day later than its last judgement, passes a later `check`.\n   320\t11. **Builder end to end,** run as the user calls it (subprocess, `--as-of` omitted). The package is final and passes `check`.\n   321\t12. **Builder refusal, through the real command, on a scratch copy** (the AGENTS §4 mutation procedure; no fake in the suite):\n   322\t    - the unchanged command succeeds on the fixture store (test 11);\n   323\t    - on a scratch copy, the writer fault \"one evidence `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`\" is introduced.\n   324\t      The same command exits 1 with the origin-mismatch reason, no `--out` and no staging folder left;\n   325\t    - on a second scratch copy, the same writer fault plus the builder's staged check removed: the bad package reaches `--out`. That\n   326\t      shows the staged check is what prevents publication.\n   327\t13. **`check` with a missing item.** A finished package. Then a copy of the items database with one referenced item deleted, and a\n   328\t    copy of the package with that same source removed and its manifest hash refreshed. `check` refuses, naming the missing item. (An\n   329\t    inner-join mutant accepts this pair, so this case catches it.)\n   330\t14. **The publication rule.**\n   331\t    - Module steps: builds A and B both stage, then A publishes. B's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`. A's package passes `check`, and\n   332\t      B's staging is still there for its owner to remove.\n   333\t    - Module steps: after staging, a foreign *empty* folder is put at `--out`. `publish` refuses, and the foreign folder still exists\n   334\t      afterwards, empty.\n   335\t    - The command, early: an existing empty `--out` gives exit 1, and the folder survives.\n   336\t    - The command, late (a scratch copy with a pause before `publish`, released by the test): the test creates an empty folder at\n   337\t      `--out` during the pause. The command exits 1, its staging folder is removed, and the same empty folder survives (same device\n   338\t      and inode).\n   339\t    - The command, after the move (a scratch copy with a pause just after `publish`): the test recreates the freed staging name as a\n   340\t      folder holding a marker file. After the command exits 0, the marker is still there.\n   341\t17. **A database error through the command.** A valid ledger with an items database that has no `items` table: exit 1, the database\n   342\t    error printed, nothing at `--out`, no staging folder left. A retry at the same `--out` with the correct items database succeeds.\n   343\t15. **Files:**\n   344\t    - a symbolic link in place of `release-data.json` fails;\n   345\t    - a data file whose repeated `one_line` member has the genuine value last, with the manifest hash refreshed so every other\n   346\t      check passes, fails on the repeated name.\n   347\t16. **Bound validation:** `2026-08-99` refused; a valid day before the first question gives an empty package.\n   348\t\n   349\t**Mutants,** on a scratch copy with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; each must fail a test:\n   350\t- `condition` emitted on number records;\n   351\t- `one_line` taken from the latest judgement's `why_changed`;\n   352\t- the event test removed;\n   353\t- the Yes/No test removed;\n   354\t- `check_package` without the file-set check;\n   355\t- manifest keys unchecked;\n   356\t- `check_export` without the closed-key check;\n   357\t- `check_origins` skipping evidence fields;\n   358\t- `check_origins` taking the class from the package;\n   359\t- `check_origins` comparing sets instead of ordered lists;\n   360\t- `check_origins` with an inner join to `items`;\n   361\t- `check` without validating the package's `as_of` against the store;\n   362\t- the builder skipping the staged `check_package` (the scratch-copy pair in test 12);\n   363\t- `publish` replaced by `os.rename` (test 14's foreign empty folder is then replaced);\n   364\t- the `finally` removed (test 17 then leaves staging);\n   365\t- the staging path not dropped after `publish` (test 14's marker is then removed);\n   366\t- the symbolic-link check removed;\n   367\t- the duplicate-key check removed;\n   368\t- the switch reason emitted;\n   369\t- the missing-item refusal replaced by the id fallback.\n   370\t\n   371\t## 7. The $0 release check (stored stores, read-only)\n   372\t\n   373\tStores: `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` (`comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-N/prod/views.sqlite`, items `items-comparison.sqlite`) and the\n   374\tserved ledger with its items database.\n   375\t\n   376\t**Budgets,** set before the first control (AGENTS §2):\n   377\t- the package's data bytes at most `bundle.library`'s JSON bytes on the same store and bound;\n   378\t- export plus all checks at most three times `bundle.library`'s seconds on the same store, and at most 120 s per store.\n   379\t\n   380\tThe steps:\n   381\t1. **Build each store's package at its default bound.** The build passes `check_package` with `check_origins`. Report the fields\n   382\t   compared, the counts per class and the unresolved list.\n   383\t2. **The decisive acceptance case** (council 74), on the `old-1` package:\n   384\t   - Morningstar's `$361 billion` estimate (`e2295`) is kept, its summary and quote equal to the stored ones;\n   385\t   - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`) is kept;\n   386\t   - the genuine analyst \"$390 billion\" quote (`e3597`) is kept, as the control;\n   387\t   - in a copy of the staged package, the system's `old-1` j1580 `implied_outcome` (\"About $390 billion…\") substituted into\n   388\t     `e2295`'s summary fails `check_origins`;\n   389\t   - the same text added to the manifest fails `check_package`.\n   390\t3. **`old-1/v8`:** `class` is `number`, with the marker and the same evidence ids as `service.evidence` at the bound.\n   391\t4. **The known event leaks at their own dates.** Export `old-3` at 2026-08-25 (`v36` j799 is the latest judgement) and `old-1` at\n   392\t   2026-08-28 (`v10` j865). Each keeps its original answer label, and j799's \"around $1 trillion\" text and j865's band text are absent.\n   393\t5. **Control:** one unchanged event question keeps its label and evidence.\n   394\t6. **Closing.** On a temporary copy of `old-1`, add a closing switch for `v8` in the store's own format (\"due …, frozen on … at\n   395\t   rung N <label>\"). First confirm that `bundle.view_bundle` exposes the reason with the band label. Then confirm the package shows\n   396\t   `open: false` and not the reason.\n   397\t7. **Diagnostics** (not the gate). For every question, take each string the package must not hold:\n   398\t   - rung labels and conditions;\n   399\t   - judgement `reasons` and `why_changed`, and `implied_outcome` and `reference` where the store has those columns (the served\n   400\t     ledger has neither; the report says so);\n   401\t   - switch reasons.\n   402\t\n   403\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\n   404\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \"Bullish\", is recorded as such.\n   405\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\n   406\t\n   407\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\n   408\t\n   409\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\n   410\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \"more than $40 billion in\n   411\tFY2028\" for a quote's \"more than double that next year\".\n   412\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\n   413\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\n   414\t  sentence. One restates \"close to doubling\" as \"nearly 100%\".\n   415\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\n   416\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \"takes\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\n   417\t  judged position.\n   418\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\n   419\t  reproduces.\n   420\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\n   421\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \"amounts as quoted\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\n   422\t    as `e3238`'s \"more than $40 billion\".\n   423\t  - Claude reads it as \"the release computes or converts nothing\".\n   424\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\n   425\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\n   426\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\n   427\t  allow-list or change it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'wc -lc docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md; nl -ba docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md'","aggregated_output":"     201   26537 docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\n     427   30421 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md\n     628   56958 total\n     1\t# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n     2\t\n     3\t> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n     4\t> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n     5\t> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n     6\t> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n     7\t> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n     8\t> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n     9\t> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n    10\t> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n    11\t\n    12\t## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n    13\t\n    14\tBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n    15\t\n    16\t1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n    17\t2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n    18\t3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n    19\t   word for it is already given.\n    20\t4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n    21\t   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n    22\t5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n    23\t   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n    24\t\n    25\t## 1. Goal (end to end)\n    26\t\n    27\tEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\n    28\tnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\n    29\tany one step's own score.\n    30\t\n    31\t## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n    32\t\n    33\t**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n    34\t\n    35\tThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n    36\t\n    37\t- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n    38\t  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n    39\t  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n    40\t  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n    41\t  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n    42\t- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n    43\t  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n    44\t  nothing at all and were never judged.\n    45\t\n    46\t**Evidence:**\n    47\t\n    48\t| Evidence | Content | Source |\n    49\t|---|---|---|\n    50\t| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n    51\t| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n    52\t| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n    53\t| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n    54\t\n    55\tAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n    56\t\n    57\t## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n    58\t\n    59\t| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n    60\t|---|---|---|\n    61\t| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n    62\t| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n    63\t| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n    64\t| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n    65\t| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n    66\t| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n    67\t| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n    68\t| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n    69\t\n    70\t## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n    71\t\n    72\t- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n    73\t  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n    74\t  system (D263).\n    75\t- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n    76\t  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n    77\t  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n    78\t- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n    79\t- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n    80\t  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n    81\t  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n    82\t  competition or pricing\".\n    83\t- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n    84\t  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n    85\t  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n    86\t  of the previous filing topic).\n    87\t- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n    88\t  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n    89\t  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n    90\t  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n    91\t- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n    92\t\n    93\t## 5. What to do\n    94\t\n    95\tStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n    96\t\n    97\t1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n    98\t   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n    99\t   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   100\t   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n   101\t     the existing rule).\n   102\t   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   103\t   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   104\t   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   105\t   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n   106\t     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n   107\t2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   108\t   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   109\t   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   110\t   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   111\t   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   112\t   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   113\t   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   114\t   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n   115\t3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   116\t   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n   117\t4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   118\t   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n   119\t\n   120\t## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n   121\t\n   122\t- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n   123\t  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n   124\t  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n   125\t- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n   126\t  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n   127\t  measured and reported apart.\n   128\t- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n   129\t- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n   130\t  counted after.\n   131\t- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n   132\t  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n   133\t  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n   134\t  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n   135\t    question\";\n   136\t  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n   137\t  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n   138\t  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n   139\t    or no question uses);\n   140\t  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n   141\t  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n   142\t    ones that matter one by one.\n   143\t- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n   144\t  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n   145\t  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n   146\t  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n   147\t    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n   148\t    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n   149\t      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n   150\t    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n   151\t      facts must not fall.\n   152\t  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n   153\t    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n   154\t      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n   155\t      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n   156\t      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n   157\t    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n   158\t      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n   159\t    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n   160\t      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n   161\t      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n   162\t      what was measured.\n   163\t  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n   164\t    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n   165\t  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n   166\t  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n   167\t\n   168\t## 7. Process (no drift)\n   169\t\n   170\t- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n   171\t  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n   172\t  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n   173\t- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n   174\t- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n   175\t  sentence, in both directions.\n   176\t- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n   177\t- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n   178\t\n   179\t## 8. Steps and where we are\n   180\t\n   181\t| # | Step | Output | Status |\n   182\t|---|---|---|---|\n   183\t| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n   184\t| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n   185\t| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n   186\t| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n   187\t| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n   188\t| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n   189\t| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n   190\t| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n   191\t| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n   192\t\n   193\t## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n   194\t\n   195\t- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n   196\t- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n   197\t- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n   198\t- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n   199\t- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n   200\t- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n   201\t- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round74-brief.md; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74e.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Council round 74: review the slice-1 build design before any code (read-only)\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\n     4\t\n     5\t## What to review\n     6\t\n     7\t`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`, the build design for the first slice of the \"Forecast unavailable\"\n     8\trelease. The governing documents:\n     9\t- `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` (revision 4, ready per `codex-r72d.md`);\n    10\t- D726, D756, D757 and D758 at the end of `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`;\n    11\t- AGENTS.md §2 (design tables before code), §3 (one owner; the writer refuses), §4 (tests) and §5.\n    12\t\n    13\tCode that the design reuses:\n    14\t- `src/hivemind/service.py`: `resolve_bound`, `view_exists`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `evidence`, `evidence_record`,\n    15\t  `ladder_bands`;\n    16\t- `src/hivemind/bundle.py`: `read_snapshot`, `item_lookup`, `view_bundle`;\n    17\t- `src/hivemind/views/store.py`: `view_key`, `rungs_of`;\n    18\t- `src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10`;\n    19\t- `src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24`;\n    20\t- `src/hivemind/idea.py`, for the idea question.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Questions\n    23\t\n    24\t1. **Leaks.** Does the allow-list in §1 let any number forecast reach the package? Check:\n    25\t   - each allowed field's real content in stored stores, read-only (for example `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`):\n    26\t     `question`, evidence `one_line` and `quote`, source titles;\n    27\t   - whether evidence linked to a number question can itself be a system-written forecast rather than a source statement.\n    28\t\n    29\t   Name any path with a stored example.\n    30\t2. **Tables.** Are the state × event, value × reader and new path × old checks tables complete? Name any blank or wrong cell, for\n    31\t   example an event the export can meet that is not listed.\n    32\t3. **Tests and mutants.** Does each named test fail without the code it tests? Is a decisive case missing?\n    33\t4. **The $0 release check (§7).** Is the leak sweep sound? Consider the 12-character floor and the string classes. Would it miss a\n    34\t   forecast restated in different words?\n    35\t5. **The four open points in §8:**\n    36\t   - no idea submission in the release, with the idea acceptance moved to a later slice;\n    37\t   - `object` and `kind` on every record;\n    38\t   - groups left out;\n    39\t   - the sweep floor.\n    40\t\n    41\t   Decide each.\n    42\t6. **Ready to build?** Give a verdict: ready, or not ready with each serious finding.\n    43\t\n    44\t**Out of scope:** the judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen); the closed v13s line; the POC's own behaviour; any other open\n    45\tdefect; wording. Report only findings that change what is built or whether it is safe.\n     1\t**Not ready to build.** Revision 5 closes both 74d defects at `--out`. Two issues remain. Test 14 checks the command’s exit status on the wrong path, and cleanup can delete a directory that reuses the staging name after publication.\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Both 74d defects are closed in the design.** The only operation that creates `--out` is an atomic move that refuses an existing destination, including an empty directory. A database error before that move leaves only private staging to clean up. Test 17 specifies the missing-table error, exit 1, absence of both output and staging, and a successful retry at the same path. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:142) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:171](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:171) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:329](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:329)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **Test 14 still misses the command’s late refusal.** Its module test creates the foreign empty directory after staging. Its command test creates the directory before startup, so the early check can return exit 1 without ever reaching `publish` or staging cleanup. Run the real command on a scratch copy with a pause immediately before `publish`, create the empty directory, then resume. Assert exit 1, removal of the build’s staging folder, and survival of the same empty directory by device and inode. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:161](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:161) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:212) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:326](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:326) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:328](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:328)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **Revision 5 introduces a cleanup race at the old staging name.** Once `publish` succeeds, the rename frees that name. If another process creates a directory there before `finally` runs, the specified “if it still exists” check can remove the new directory. End the build’s cleanup responsibility as soon as the move succeeds. The decisive test recreates the old staging directory with a marker file after the move and verifies that the marker survives command exit. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:138](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:138) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:163](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:163) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:167)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
