\\''v8'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v38'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''v15'\\\\\\\\'']:\\n   v=c.execute(\\\\\\\"select question,measure from views join view_keys using(view_id) where view_id=?\\\\\\\",(t,)).fetchone()\\n   print(t,tuple(v) if v else None)\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"old-1 source values 1223 empty {'id': 0, 'title': 0, 'publisher': 0, 'uri': 0}\\nv8 ('How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 'segment_revenue')\\nv38 ('How much will NVIDIA’s MediaTek convertible-bond purchase obligation amount to at the FY2027 annual report?', 'financing_amount')\\nv15 ('How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 'product_revenue')\\nold-2 source values 1241 empty {'id': 0, 'title': 0, 'publisher': 0, 'uri': 0}\\nv8 ('How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?', 'other')\\nv38 ('Will NVIDIA complete an investment of roughly $2.5 billion to $3 billion in Thinking Machines Lab by 2027-09-04?', 'event')\\nv15 (\\\"How much will NVIDIA's supply commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\\\", 'financing_amount')\\nold-3 source values 1286 empty {'id': 0, 'title': 0, 'publisher': 0, 'uri': 0}\\nserved source values 746 empty {'id': 0, 'title': 0, 'publisher': 0, 'uri': 0}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:92:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_47\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\\nroot=Path(\\\\\\\"poc/data\\\\\\\")\\nbase=root/\\\\\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\\\\\"\\ndef conn(p):\\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\\\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\\\\\",uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\ninputs=[(f\\\\\\\"old-{i}\\\\\\\",base/f\\\\\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\\\\\",base/\\\\\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\\\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\\\\\"served\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\\\\\")]\\nfor n,vid in [(1,\\\\\\\"v38\\\\\\\"),(2,\\\\\\\"v33\\\\\\\")]:\\n name,p,ip=inputs[n];c=conn(p);i=conn(ip)\\n r=c.execute(\\\\\\\"select question,created_from_input,created_seq from views where view_id=?\\\\\\\",(vid,)).fetchone(); a=i.execute(\\\\\\\"select title,publisher,text from items where input_id=?\\\\\\\",(r[1],)).fetchone()\\n print(name,vid,tuple(r),a[0]); print(a[2][:1080])\\n print(\\\\\\\"j first\\\\\\\",tuple(c.execute(\\\\\\\"select seq,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id limit 1\\\\\\\",(vid,)).fetchone()))\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.stream:93:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_47\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\\nimport sqlite3,collections,re,sys,json\\nroot=Path(\\\\\\\"poc/data\\\\\\\")\\nbase=root/\\\\\\\"comparison-2026-11-17\\\\\\\"\\ndef conn(p):\\n c=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\\\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\\\\\",uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\ninputs=[(f\\\\\\\"old-{i}\\\\\\\",base/f\\\\\\\"run/old-{i}/prod/views.sqlite\\\\\\\",base/\\\\\\\"items-comparison.sqlite\\\\\\\") for i in (1,2,3)]+[(\\\\\\\"served\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\"served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite\\\\\\\",root/\\\\\\\"items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite\\\\\\\")]\\nfor n,vid in [(1,\\\\\\\"v38\\\\\\\"),(2,\\\\\\\"v33\\\\\\\")]:\\n name,p,ip=inputs[n];c=conn(p);i=conn(ip)\\n r=c.execute(\\\\\\\"select question,created_from_input,created_seq from views where view_id=?\\\\\\\",(vid,)).fetchone(); a=i.execute(\\\\\\\"select title,publisher,text from items where input_id=?\\\\\\\",(r[1],)).fetchone()\\n print(name,vid,tuple(r),a[0]); print(a[2][:1080])\\n print(\\\\\\\"j first\\\\\\\",tuple(c.execute(\\\\\\\"select seq,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id=? order by judgement_id limit 1\\\\\\\",(vid,)).fetchone()))\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"old-2 v38 ('Will NVIDIA complete an investment of roughly $2.5 billion to $3 billion in Thinking Machines Lab by 2027-09-04?', 'gnews:21017fa01f34cb308af3b38b', 1394) Nvidia Is Eyeing a $2.5 Billion Bet on Mira Murati's AI Startup\\nNvidia Corp. ( NVDA , Financials ), the dominant supplier of artificial intelligence chips, could put roughly $2.5 billion into Mira Murati's Thinking Machines Lab as it expands its reach beyond selling hardware.\\nThinking Machines is in talks to raise between $5 billion and $6 billion at a valuation of at least $40 billion before the new investment, according to The Information.\\nNvidia is expected to provide roughly half of that capital. The potential deal would deepen an already close relationship.\\nIn March, Nvidia and Thinking Machines announced a multiyear partnership to deploy at least 1 gigawatt of next-generation Vera Rubin systems. The first deployment is targeted for early next year. That makes the investment strategically different from a typical venture bet.\\nNvidia would be helping finance an AI company that has already committed to deploying its infrastructure at enormous scale. The arrangement could strengthen future demand for Nvidia systems while giving Thinking Machines access to the computing capacity needed to build and serve advanced AI models.\\nT\\nj first (1429, 'Rung 1 (Yes): if the reported $5–6 billion fundraising closes, NVIDIA’s expected roughly half would imply an investment of about $2.5–3 billion, within the question’s amount and due-date scope. The report does not specify the fundraising period or confirm completion, but the due date is one year away and the stated expectation makes completion by then the likelier outcome.')\\nold-3 v33 ('At NVIDIA’s FY2027 annual filing, what amount of equity investment commitments will NVIDIA report as outstanding or committed?', 'gnews:d024d71d75661d369798d307', 821) Nvidia's $70 billion bet on OpenAI, Anthropic, and others could pay off big for shareholders\\nArguably, no one has more at stake than Nvidia ( NVDA ) in the AI boom.\\nNext-gen companies such as Elon Musk's SpaceX ( SPCX ) are clamoring for Nvidia's high-powered computing chips , which are at the heart of the investment thesis on the company.\\nBut investors should also consider the formidable investment portfolio Nvidia now holds. When companies like OpenAI ( OPAI.PVT ) and Anthropic ( ANTH.PVT ) inevitably go public at stratospheric valuations within the next year, Nvidia's early backing of these companies stands to drive additional value for its shareholders.\\nNvidia has committed to directly providing $70 billion in equity investments into ecosystem partners, per new research from Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya. Recent investments include $30 billion in OpenAI, up to $10 billion in Anthropic, and $5 billion in Safe Superintelligence.\\n\\\"Overall, we view Nvidia's $70 billion investments as easily manageable given its ability to generate as much as about $470 billion of free cash flow over just the next two years (2026-2027), or about 15% of free cash flow,\\nj first (834, 'About $70 billion of equity investment commitments, based on Arya’s estimate that NVIDIA has committed that amount to ecosystem partners; the estimate’s period is unspecified, but it is stated as commitments already made. That amount reaches the rung-5 boundary of $70 billion.')\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba scripts/mock_build.py\\nnl -ba poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js\\nnl -ba poc/ui/prepare-data.mjs\\nnl -ba scripts/mock_translate.py | head -140'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"Validate data and bundle the modular Thesis UI into the portable mock HTML.\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tInstall build dependencies once with ``npm ci --prefix poc/ui``. No model or network\\n     4\\tcalls are made by this build. Existing source data and translation caches are not changed.\\n     5\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     6\\timport argparse\\n     7\\timport json\\n     8\\tfrom pathlib import Path\\n     9\\timport subprocess\\n    10\\timport sys\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\n    13\\tsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'src'))\\n    14\\tfrom hivemind import bundle, service  # noqa: E402\\n    15\\tfrom hivemind.views import store  # noqa: E402\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tdef main():\\n    19\\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\\n    20\\t    parser.add_argument('--data', type=Path, help='explicit legacy JSON export; otherwise read the current ledger')\\n    21\\t    parser.add_argument('--ledger', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite')\\n    22\\t    parser.add_argument('--items', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite')\\n    23\\t    parser.add_argument('--out', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/mock/index.html')\\n    24\\t    parser.add_argument('--composite-trials', type=Path, help='explicit JSON trial baskets for the Idea score preview')\\n    25\\t    parser.add_argument('--market-data', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/ui/data/nvda-2026-10-27.json', help='dated real stock-price snapshot for the Action preview')\\n    26\\t    args = parser.parse_args()\\n    27\\t    if args.data:\\n    28\\t        data = json.loads(args.data.read_text())\\n    29\\t    else:\\n    30\\t        conn, items = service.open_ledger(str(args.ledger)), store.open_read_only(str(args.items))\\n    31\\t        try:\\n    32\\t            data = bundle.library(conn, items)\\n    33\\t        finally:\\n    34\\t            conn.close()\\n    35\\t            items.close()\\n    36\\t    if args.data and not data.get('schema_version') and args.ledger.exists():\\n    37\\t        conn = service.open_ledger(str(args.ledger))\\n    38\\t        try:\\n    39\\t            data['sequence_days'] = service.seq_day_map(conn)\\n    40\\t        finally:\\n    41\\t            conn.close()\\n    42\\t    ui = ROOT / 'poc/ui'\\n    43\\t    bundled = subprocess.run(['node', str(ui / 'build.mjs'), '--json'], capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    44\\t    if bundled.returncode:\\n    45\\t        print('UI build failed. Install its pinned dependencies with: npm ci --prefix poc/ui', file=sys.stderr)\\n    46\\t        print(bundled.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\\n    47\\t        bundled.check_returncode()\\n    48\\t    built = json.loads(bundled.stdout)\\n    49\\t    prepared = subprocess.run(['node', str(ui / 'prepare-data.mjs')], input=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False), capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    50\\t    if prepared.returncode:\\n    51\\t        print(prepared.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\\n    52\\t        prepared.check_returncode()\\n    53\\t    print(prepared.stderr.strip())\\n    54\\t    market = subprocess.run(['node', str(ui / 'prepare-data.mjs'), '--market'], input=args.market_data.read_text(), capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    55\\t    if market.returncode:\\n    56\\t        print(market.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\\n    57\\t        market.check_returncode()\\n    58\\t    print(market.stderr.strip())\\n    59\\t    template = (ROOT / 'poc/mock/index.template.html').read_text()\\n    60\\t    page = template.replace('__STYLES__', built['style']).replace('__SCRIPT__', built['script'].replace('</script', '<\\\\\\\\/script'))\\n    61\\t    page = page.replace('__DATA__', prepared.stdout.replace('<', '\\\\\\\\u003c'))\\n    62\\t    page = page.replace('__MARKET_DATA__', market.stdout.replace('<', '\\\\\\\\u003c'))\\n    63\\t    trials = json.loads(args.composite_trials.read_text()) if args.composite_trials else []\\n    64\\t    page = page.replace('__COMPOSITE_TRIALS__', json.dumps(trials, ensure_ascii=False).replace('<', '\\\\\\\\u003c'))\\n    65\\t    output = args.out.resolve()\\n    66\\t    output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    67\\t    temporary = output.with_suffix(output.suffix + '.tmp')\\n    68\\t    temporary.write_text(page)\\n    69\\t    temporary.replace(output)\\n    70\\t    print(f'UI: {len(built[\\\"script\\\"].encode()):,} JS bytes; wrote {output} ({len(page.encode()):,} bytes)')\\n    71\\t\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\tif __name__ == '__main__':\\n    74\\t    main()\\n     1\\timport { createThesisExplorer, createLibrary } from './index.js';\\n     2\\timport { fromBundles } from './adapters/bundle.js';\\n     3\\timport { parseDataset } from './model/contract.js';\\n     4\\timport { readIdea, readBundles, idsOf, graphOf, ideaCard } from './idea/idea.js';\\n     5\\timport { score, undirected } from './model/thesis.js';\\n     6\\timport { createIdeaDetail } from './idea/analysis.js';\\n     7\\timport {\\n     8\\t  prepareCompositeTrial,\\n     9\\t  prepareIdeaComposite,\\n    10\\t  compositeAt,\\n    11\\t  confidenceFromScore,\\n    12\\t  CompositeUnavailable,\\n    13\\t} from './idea/composite.js';\\n    14\\timport { DEFAULT_TRIGGER_CONDITION } from './model/trigger.js';\\n    15\\timport { advanceIdeaProgress } from './idea/progress.js';\\n    16\\timport { createIdeaComposer } from './components/idea-composer.js';\\n    17\\timport { DEFAULT_ACTION_SETTINGS } from './model/market.js';\\n    18\\texport * from './index.js';\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\tconst API = document.body.dataset.api || 'http://127.0.0.1:8788';\\n    21\\tconst input = document.getElementById('ask');\\n    22\\tconst root = document.getElementById('explorer');\\n    23\\tconst libraryRoot = document.getElementById('library');\\n    24\\tif (input && root && libraryRoot) {\\n    25\\t  try {\\n    26\\t    const initial = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('data').textContent);\\n    27\\t    let data = initial.schema_version ? parseDataset(initial) : fromBundles(initial);\\n    28\\t    const compositeTrials = JSON.parse(\\n    29\\t      document.getElementById('composite-trials')?.textContent || '[]',\\n    30\\t    );\\n    31\\t    // Explicit old exports remain usable for standalone component previews.\\n    32\\t    const library = createLibrary(libraryRoot, { dataset: data });\\n    33\\t    let app = null;\\n    34\\t    let inFlight = null;\\n    35\\t    let requestNumber = 0;\\n    36\\t    let deferredPresentation = null;\\n    37\\t    let leadingDirty = false;\\n    38\\t    const libraryRequest = new AbortController();\\n    39\\t    const form = document.getElementById('idea-form');\\n    40\\t    const send = document.getElementById('idea-send');\\n    41\\t    const composer = createIdeaComposer({\\n    42\\t      root,\\n    43\\t      form,\\n    44\\t      input,\\n    45\\t      launcher: document.getElementById('idea-launcher'),\\n    46\\t    });\\n    47\\t    const libraryButton = document.getElementById('show-library');\\n    48\\t    const ideaButton = document.getElementById('show-idea');\\n    49\\t    const idea = { text: '', state: 'idle', card: null, error: null };\\n    50\\t    let market = null;\\n    51\\t    try {\\n    52\\t      market = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('market-data')?.textContent || 'null');\\n    53\\t    } catch {\\n    54\\t      /* The card renders unavailable prices. */\\n    55\\t    }\\n    56\\t    const action = {\\n    57\\t      market,\\n    58\\t      settings: { ...DEFAULT_ACTION_SETTINGS },\\n    59\\t      onChange: (settings) => {\\n    60\\t        action.settings = settings;\\n    61\\t      },\\n    62\\t    };\\n    63\\t    const trigger = {\\n    64\\t      condition: { ...DEFAULT_TRIGGER_CONDITION },\\n    65\\t      getConfidence: () =>\\n    66\\t        idea.composite\\n    67\\t          ? confidenceFromScore(compositeAt(idea.composite, idea.day)?.value ?? null)\\n    68\\t          : null,\\n    69\\t      onChange: (condition) => {\\n    70\\t        trigger.condition = condition;\\n    71\\t      },\\n    72\\t    };\\n    73\\t    const ideaDetail = createIdeaDetail({ root: document.body });\\n    74\\t    function updateSendState() {\\n    75\\t      send.disabled = !input.value.trim() || Boolean(inFlight);\\n    76\\t      form.setAttribute('aria-busy', String(Boolean(inFlight)));\\n    77\\t    }\\n    78\\t    function cancelIdea() {\\n    79\\t      inFlight?.abort();\\n    80\\t      inFlight = null;\\n    81\\t      requestNumber++;\\n    82\\t      updateSendState();\\n    83\\t    }\\n    84\\t    function showLibrary() {\\n    85\\t      ideaDetail.close();\\n    86\\t      app?.pause();\\n    87\\t      root.hidden = true;\\n    88\\t      libraryRoot.hidden = false;\\n    89\\t      libraryButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\\n    90\\t      ideaButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');\\n    91\\t    }\\n    92\\t    function showIdea() {\\n    93\\t      library.close();\\n    94\\t      libraryRoot.hidden = true;\\n    95\\t      root.hidden = false;\\n    96\\t      libraryButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');\\n    97\\t      ideaButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\\n    98\\t      const firstVisit = !app;\\n    99\\t      if (firstVisit) {\\n   100\\t        app = createThesisExplorer(root, {\\n   101\\t          dataset: data,\\n   102\\t          onDayChange: (day, range) => {\\n   103\\t            idea.day = day;\\n   104\\t            idea.chartStart = range?.start;\\n   105\\t          },\\n   106\\t        });\\n   107\\t        app.showGraph({ day: library.getDay() });\\n   108\\t      }\\n   109\\t      if (deferredPresentation) {\\n   110\\t        const { spec, dataset } = deferredPresentation;\\n   111\\t        present(spec, dataset);\\n   112\\t      } else if (leadingDirty) {\\n   113\\t        app.updateLeading();\\n   114\\t        leadingDirty = false;\\n   115\\t      }\\n   116\\t      if (firstVisit) composer.open();\\n   117\\t      updateSendState();\\n   118\\t    }\\n   119\\t    function present(spec, dataset = null) {\\n   120\\t      if (root.hidden) {\\n   121\\t        deferredPresentation = { spec, dataset };\\n   122\\t        return;\\n   123\\t      }\\n   124\\t      if (dataset) app.setDataset(dataset);\\n   125\\t      app.showGraph({ ...spec, ...(idea.state === 'answered' ? { trigger, action } : {}) });\\n   126\\t      deferredPresentation = null;\\n   127\\t      leadingDirty = false;\\n   128\\t    }\\n   129\\t    const leadingCard = (layout = {}) =>\\n   130\\t      ideaCard({\\n   131\\t        ...idea,\\n   132\\t        ...layout,\\n   133\\t        onOpen: () =>\\n   134\\t          ideaDetail.open(idea.card, data.theses, idea.composite, idea.day, idea.createdDay),\\n   135\\t        scoreOf: (position) => {\\n   136\\t          const thesis = app\\n   137\\t            ?.getDataset()\\n   138\\t            .theses.find((t) => t.id === idea.card?.reading?.chosen[0]?.view_id);\\n   139\\t          if (!thesis) return `position ${position}`;\\n   140\\t          return undirected(thesis)\\n   141\\t            ? (thesis.rungs.find((r) => r.position === position)?.label ?? `position ${position}`)\\n   142\\t            : score(thesis, position);\\n   143\\t        },\\n   144\\t      });\\n   145\\t    async function run(event) {\\n   146\\t      event.preventDefault();\\n   147\\t      const text = input.value.trim();\\n   148\\t      if (!text || inFlight) return;\\n   149\\t      deferredPresentation = null;\\n   150\\t      leadingDirty = false;\\n   151\\t      trigger.condition = { ...DEFAULT_TRIGGER_CONDITION };\\n   152\\t      action.settings = { ...DEFAULT_ACTION_SETTINGS };\\n   153\\t      composer.close();\\n   154\\t      input.value = '';\\n   155\\t      ideaDetail.close();\\n   156\\t      cancelIdea();\\n   157\\t      const mine = ++requestNumber;\\n   158\\t      inFlight = new AbortController();\\n   159\\t      updateSendState();\\n   160\\t      const signal = inFlight.signal;\\n   161\\t      const submitted = new Date();\\n   162\\t      const createdDay = [\\n   163\\t        submitted.getFullYear(),\\n   164\\t        String(submitted.getMonth() + 1).padStart(2, '0'),\\n   165\\t        String(submitted.getDate()).padStart(2, '0'),\\n   166\\t      ].join('-');\\n   167\\t      Object.assign(idea, {\\n   168\\t        text,\\n   169\\t        createdDay,\\n   170\\t        state: 'pending',\\n   171\\t        card: null,\\n   172\\t        error: null,\\n   173\\t        composite: null,\\n   174\\t        day: library.getDay(),\\n   175\\t        chartStart: undefined,\\n   176\\t        progress: ['search'],\\n   177\\t      });\\n   178\\t      app.showGraph({\\n   179\\t        day: library.getDay(),\\n   180\\t        leadingCard,\\n   181\\t        centerOn: 'tree',\\n   182\\t        center: true,\\n   183\\t      });\\n   184\\t      try {\\n   185\\t        const updateProgress = (stage) => {\\n   186\\t          if (mine !== requestNumber || signal.aborted) return;\\n   187\\t          const progress = advanceIdeaProgress(idea.progress, stage);\\n   188\\t          if (progress === idea.progress) return;\\n   189\\t          idea.progress = progress;\\n   190\\t          if (root.hidden) leadingDirty = true;\\n   191\\t          else app.updateLeading();\\n   192\\t        };\\n   193\\t        const card = await readIdea(API, text, {\\n   194\\t          signal,\\n   195\\t          asOf: library.getDay(),\\n   196\\t          onProgress: updateProgress,\\n   197\\t        });\\n   198\\t        if (mine !== requestNumber) return;\\n   199\\t        updateProgress('cards');\\n   200\\t        const bundles = await readBundles(API, idsOf(card), card.idea.as_of, { signal });\\n   201\\t        if (mine !== requestNumber) return;\\n   202\\t        const next = bundles ? fromBundles(bundles) : null;\\n   203\\t        const chartData = next || { as_of: card.idea.as_of, days: card.days, theses: [] };\\n   204\\t        let composite = null,\\n   205\\t          compositeNote = '';\\n   206\\t        try {\\n   207\\t          composite =\\n   208\\t            prepareIdeaComposite(card, chartData) ||\\n   209\\t            (next ? prepareCompositeTrial(compositeTrials, card, next) : null);\\n   210\\t        } catch (error) {\\n   211\\t          if (!(error instanceof CompositeUnavailable)) throw error;\\n   212\\t          compositeNote = error.message; // the Idea stays; only its composite is not computed\\n   213\\t        }\\n   214\\t        Object.assign(idea, {\\n   215\\t          card,\\n   216\\t          state: 'answered',\\n   217\\t          day: card.idea.as_of,\\n   218\\t          composite,\\n   219\\t          compositeNote,\\n   220\\t        });\\n   221\\t        const weightPercents = ['idea-composite/3', 'idea-composite/4'].includes(\\n   222\\t          idea.composite?.version,\\n   223\\t        )\\n   224\\t          ? Object.fromEntries(\\n   225\\t              [...idea.composite.drivers, ...idea.composite.excluded].map((entry) => [\\n   226\\t                entry.thesis_id,\\n   227\\t                entry.weight_percent,\\n   228\\t              ]),\\n   229\\t            )\\n   230\\t          : undefined;\\n   231\\t        present(\\n   232\\t          {\\n   233\\t            ...graphOf(card),\\n   234\\t            day: card.idea.as_of,\\n   235\\t            leadingCard,\\n   236\\t            weightPercents,\\n   237\\t            centerOn: 'tree',\\n   238\\t            center: true,\\n   239\\t            reveal: true,\\n   240\\t          },\\n   241\\t          next,\\n   242\\t        );\\n   243\\t      } catch (error) {\\n   244\\t        if (error.name === 'AbortError' || mine !== requestNumber) return;\\n   245\\t        Object.assign(idea, { state: 'failed', error });\\n   246\\t        present({ leadingCard, centerOn: 'tree', center: true });\\n   247\\t      } finally {\\n   248\\t        if (mine === requestNumber) {\\n   249\\t          inFlight = null;\\n   250\\t          updateSendState();\\n   251\\t        }\\n   252\\t      }\\n   253\\t    }\\n   254\\t    async function loadLibrary() {\\n   255\\t      try {\\n   256\\t        const response = await fetch(`${API}/library`, { signal: libraryRequest.signal });\\n   257\\t        if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Service returned ${response.status}`);\\n   258\\t        const next = fromBundles(await response.json());\\n   259\\t        if (next.coverage !== 'library')\\n   260\\t          throw new Error('The service did not return a complete library');\\n   261\\t        if (libraryRequest.signal.aborted) return;\\n   262\\t        library.setDataset(next, { day: next.as_of }); // the supplied snapshot defines the displayed date (thesis-ui.md)\\n   263\\t        data = next;\\n   264\\t      } catch {\\n   265\\t        // Keep the displayed snapshot when the optional live read is unavailable.\\n   266\\t      }\\n   267\\t    }\\n   268\\t    form.addEventListener('submit', run);\\n   269\\t    input.addEventListener('input', updateSendState);\\n   270\\t    libraryButton.addEventListener('click', showLibrary);\\n   271\\t    ideaButton.addEventListener('click', showIdea);\\n   272\\t    window.addEventListener(\\n   273\\t      'pagehide',\\n   274\\t      () => {\\n   275\\t        cancelIdea();\\n   276\\t        libraryRequest.abort();\\n   277\\t        library.destroy();\\n   278\\t        app?.destroy();\\n   279\\t        ideaDetail.destroy();\\n   280\\t        composer.destroy();\\n   281\\t      },\\n   282\\t      { once: true },\\n   283\\t    );\\n   284\\t    showLibrary();\\n   285\\t    updateSendState();\\n   286\\t    loadLibrary();\\n   287\\t  } catch (error) {\\n   288\\t    const message = document.createElement('p');\\n   289\\t    message.className = 'ui-error';\\n   290\\t    message.setAttribute('role', 'alert');\\n   291\\t    message.textContent = `Cannot load the thesis data: ${error.message}`;\\n   292\\t    libraryRoot.append(message);\\n   293\\t  }\\n   294\\t}\\n     1\\timport fs from 'node:fs';\\n     2\\timport { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks';\\n     3\\timport { fromBundles } from './src/adapters/bundle.js';\\n     4\\timport { parseDataset } from './src/model/contract.js';\\n     5\\timport { readMarketSnapshot } from './src/model/market.js';\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\tconst source = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8'));\\n     8\\tconst start = performance.now();\\n     9\\tconst market = process.argv.includes('--market');\\n    10\\tconst dataset = market\\n    11\\t  ? readMarketSnapshot(source)\\n    12\\t  : source.schema_version\\n    13\\t    ? parseDataset(source)\\n    14\\t    : fromBundles(source);\\n    15\\tprocess.stderr.write(\\n    16\\t  `Validated ${market ? `${dataset.hourly.length + dataset.daily.length} price observations` : `${dataset.theses.length} theses`} in ${(performance.now() - start).toFixed(1)}ms\\\\n`,\\n    17\\t);\\n    18\\tprocess.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(dataset));\\n     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"Translate the mock's data (poc/mock/data.json, written by the pipeline in Chinese) into English for the\\n     2\\tfront-end mock, with gpt-6-luna through the same archived model call as the pipeline (a repeated run costs $0).\\n     3\\t\\n     4\\tEnumerations are mapped, not translated (tiers, view kinds, object ladder labels, judgement pushes). Everything\\n     5\\telse that the page shows is translated in batches: view questions and what they look at, ladder conditions,\\n     6\\tevidence one-liners and event times, each judgement's reasons and why-changed. Quotes, speakers, titles and dates\\n     7\\tstay as stored (quotes are the source's own words, almost all English). The Chinese ladder conditions are kept\\n     8\\tas `condition_zh` because the page reads the rung thresholds from them.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\tUsage: python3 scripts/mock_translate.py [--dry] [--limit N]   → poc/mock/data.en.json\\n    11\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    12\\timport argparse\\n    13\\timport collections\\n    14\\timport glob\\n    15\\timport json\\n    16\\timport os\\n    17\\timport re\\n    18\\timport sys\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\tROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\\n    21\\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, 'src'))\\n    22\\tfrom hivemind import config, model  # noqa: E402\\n    23\\t\\n    24\\tTIERS = {'发生的事': 'Fact', '当事人说的': 'Party statement', '第三方看法': 'Third-party view', '传闻': 'Rumour'}\\n    25\\tKINDS = {'对象观点': 'Company view', '主题观点': 'Theme view'}\\n    26\\tOBJECT_LABELS = {'强烈看多': 'Strongly bullish', '看多': 'Bullish', '中性': 'Neutral', '看空': 'Bearish', '强烈看空': 'Strongly bearish', '是': 'Yes', '否': 'No'}\\n    27\\tPUSHES = {'推向第一格': 'pushes toward rung 1', '推向最后一格': 'pushes toward rung 5', '不推': 'no push', '定格': 'settles the rung'}\\n    28\\tSCHEMA = {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['items'],\\n    29\\t          'properties': {'items': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['k', 'en'],\\n    30\\t                                                             'properties': {'k': {'type': 'string'}, 'en': {'type': 'string'}}}}}}\\n    31\\tSYSTEM = ('You translate short Chinese texts from an equity-research system into concise, natural financial English. '\\n    32\\t          'Keep every number, unit, ticker, company and product name, fiscal label (FY2027, Q1, H2) and date exactly as given. '\\n    33\\t          'Write 第 N 格 as \\\"rung N\\\" and 梯子 as \\\"ladder\\\"; 观点 is \\\"view\\\", 证据 is \\\"evidence\\\", 发生的事 is \\\"a fact\\\", 当事人说的 is \\\"a party statement\\\", '\\n    34\\t          '第三方看法 is \\\"a third-party view\\\", 传闻 is \\\"a rumour\\\". Translate questions as questions. Return one English text per key, every key, nothing else.')\\n    35\\tBATCH_CHARS = 5000\\n    36\\t\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\tdef collect(data):\\n    39\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every distinct string the page shows, keyed by a stable id -> the original text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    40\\t    todo = collections.OrderedDict()\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t    def add(key, text):\\n    43\\t        if text and text.strip():\\n    44\\t            todo[key] = text\\n    45\\t    for v in data['views']:\\n    46\\t        add(f'v:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:q', v['question'])\\n    47\\t        add(f'v:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:l', v['looks_at'])\\n    48\\t        for r in v['rungs']:\\n    49\\t            add(f'v:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:c{r[\\\"position\\\"]}', r['condition'])\\n    50\\t            if r['label'] not in OBJECT_LABELS:\\n    51\\t                add(f'v:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:r{r[\\\"position\\\"]}', r['label'])\\n    52\\t        for n, j in enumerate(v['judgements']):\\n    53\\t            add(f'j:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:{n}:why', j['why_changed'])\\n    54\\t            add(f'j:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:{n}:reasons', j['reasons'])\\n    55\\t        for e in v['evidence']:\\n    56\\t            add(f'e:{e[\\\"id\\\"]}:line', e['one_line'])\\n    57\\t            add(f'e:{e[\\\"id\\\"]}:time', e['event_time'])\\n    58\\t    return todo\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t\\n    61\\tdef batches(todo, done):\\n    62\\t    batch, size = [], 0\\n    63\\t    for key, text in todo.items():\\n    64\\t        if key in done:\\n    65\\t            continue\\n    66\\t        if batch and size + len(text) > BATCH_CHARS:\\n    67\\t            yield batch\\n    68\\t            batch, size = [], 0\\n    69\\t        batch.append((key, text))\\n    70\\t        size += len(text)\\n    71\\t    if batch:\\n    72\\t        yield batch\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\tCJK = re.compile(r'[一-鿿]')\\n    76\\tMONTHS = ['', 'Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec']\\n    77\\t\\n    78\\t\\n    79\\tdef polish(text):\\n    80\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Money and dates the model copied in Chinese units (\\\"300亿美元\\\", \\\"2026年8月26日\\\") written the English way; a\\n    81\\t    literal \\\"3500 hundred million\\\" becomes \\\"$350 billion\\\".\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    82\\t    def yi_to_dollars(match):\\n    83\\t        n = float(match.group(1).replace(',', ''))\\n    84\\t        return f'${n / 10:g} billion'\\n    85\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d[\\\\d,.]*)\\\\s*万亿美元', lambda m: f'${float(m.group(1).replace(\\\",\\\", \\\"\\\")):g} trillion', text)\\n    86\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d[\\\\d,.]*)\\\\s*亿美元', yi_to_dollars, text)\\n    87\\t    text = re.sub(r'\\\\$?(\\\\d[\\\\d,.]*)\\\\s*hundred million(?: U\\\\.S\\\\. dollars| dollars)?', yi_to_dollars, text)\\n    88\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d[\\\\d,.]*)\\\\s*万亿', lambda m: f'{float(m.group(1).replace(\\\",\\\", \\\"\\\")):g} trillion', text)\\n    89\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d[\\\\d,.]*)\\\\s*亿', lambda m: f'{float(m.group(1).replace(\\\",\\\", \\\"\\\")) / 10:g} billion', text)\\n    90\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d[\\\\d,.]*)\\\\s*美元', r'$\\\\1', text)\\n    91\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d{4})\\\\s*年\\\\s*(\\\\d{1,2})\\\\s*月\\\\s*(\\\\d{1,2})\\\\s*日', lambda m: f'{MONTHS[int(m.group(2))]} {int(m.group(3))}, {m.group(1)}', text)\\n    92\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d{4})\\\\s*年\\\\s*(\\\\d{1,2})\\\\s*月', lambda m: f'{MONTHS[int(m.group(2))]} {m.group(1)}', text)\\n    93\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d{1,2})\\\\s*月\\\\s*(\\\\d{1,2})\\\\s*日', lambda m: f'{MONTHS[int(m.group(1))]} {int(m.group(2))}', text)\\n    94\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d{4})\\\\s*年', r'\\\\1', text)\\n    95\\t    text = re.sub(r'第\\\\s*([一二三四1-4])\\\\s*季度?', lambda m: 'Q' + str('一二三四'.find(m.group(1)) + 1 if m.group(1) in '一二三四' else m.group(1)), text)\\n    96\\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\\\d[\\\\d,.]*)\\\\s*%\\\\s*', r'\\\\1% ', text)\\n    97\\t    return re.sub(r'\\\\s{2,}', ' ', text).strip()\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\tFIX_SYSTEM = SYSTEM + ' The output must contain no Chinese characters at all: write money as $X billion or $X trillion (1亿 = $0.1 billion), dates as \\\"Aug 26, 2026\\\", quarters as Q1..Q4.'\\n   101\\t\\n   102\\t\\n   103\\tdef apply(data, done):\\n   104\\t    done = {k: polish(v) for k, v in done.items()}\\n   105\\t    out = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\\n   106\\t    for v in out['views']:\\n   107\\t        v['question'] = done.get(f'v:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:q', v['question'])\\n   108\\t        v['looks_at'] = done.get(f'v:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:l', v['looks_at'])\\n   109\\t        v['kind'] = KINDS.get(v['kind'], v['kind'])\\n   110\\t        for r in v['rungs']:\\n   111\\t            r['condition_zh'] = r['condition']\\n   112\\t            r['condition'] = done.get(f'v:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:c{r[\\\"position\\\"]}', r['condition'])\\n   113\\t            r['label'] = OBJECT_LABELS.get(r['label'], done.get(f'v:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:r{r[\\\"position\\\"]}', r['label']))\\n   114\\t        for n, j in enumerate(v['judgements']):\\n   115\\t            j['why_changed'] = done.get(f'j:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:{n}:why', j['why_changed'])\\n   116\\t            j['reasons'] = done.get(f'j:{v[\\\"view_id\\\"]}:{n}:reasons', j['reasons'])\\n   117\\t            for p in j['pushes']:\\n   118\\t                p['push'] = PUSHES.get(p['push'], p['push'])\\n   119\\t        for e in v['evidence']:\\n   120\\t            e['one_line'] = done.get(f'e:{e[\\\"id\\\"]}:line', e['one_line'])\\n   121\\t            e['event_time'] = done.get(f'e:{e[\\\"id\\\"]}:time', e['event_time'])\\n   122\\t            e['tier'] = TIERS.get(e['tier'], e['tier'])\\n   123\\t    return out\\n   124\\t\\n   125\\t\\n   126\\tdef main():\\n   127\\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\n   128\\t    parser.add_argument('--data', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'mock', 'data.json'))\\n   129\\t    parser.add_argument('--out', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'mock', 'data.en.json'))\\n   130\\t    parser.add_argument('--cache', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'mock', 'translations.json'), help='key -> English, kept between runs')\\n   131\\t    parser.add_argument('--config', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118-from-v2.json'))\\n   132\\t    parser.add_argument('--archive', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'archive.sqlite'))\\n   133\\t    parser.add_argument('--dry', action='store_true')\\n   134\\t    parser.add_argument('--limit', type=int, default=0, help='stop after N batches')\\n   135\\t    parser.add_argument('--shard', default='', help='k/n: this process takes every n-th batch starting at k and writes its own cache file')\\n   136\\t    args = parser.parse_args()\\n   137\\t    with open(args.data, encoding='utf-8') as handle:\\n   138\\t        data = json.load(handle)\\n   139\\t    todo = collect(data)\\n   140\\t    # every cache file in the folder counts (one per shard), so a merge is just reading them all\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:29:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba scripts/mock_build.py | head -170\\nnl -ba poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js | head -130\\nnl -ba poc/ui/prepare-data.mjs | head -100'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"Validate data and bundle the modular Thesis UI into the portable mock HTML.\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tInstall build dependencies once with ``npm ci --prefix poc/ui``. No model or network\\n     4\\tcalls are made by this build. Existing source data and translation caches are not changed.\\n     5\\t\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     6\\timport argparse\\n     7\\timport json\\n     8\\tfrom pathlib import Path\\n     9\\timport subprocess\\n    10\\timport sys\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\n    13\\tsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / 'src'))\\n    14\\tfrom hivemind import bundle, service  # noqa: E402\\n    15\\tfrom hivemind.views import store  # noqa: E402\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tdef main():\\n    19\\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\\n    20\\t    parser.add_argument('--data', type=Path, help='explicit legacy JSON export; otherwise read the current ledger')\\n    21\\t    parser.add_argument('--ledger', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite')\\n    22\\t    parser.add_argument('--items', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite')\\n    23\\t    parser.add_argument('--out', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/mock/index.html')\\n    24\\t    parser.add_argument('--composite-trials', type=Path, help='explicit JSON trial baskets for the Idea score preview')\\n    25\\t    parser.add_argument('--market-data', type=Path, default=ROOT / 'poc/ui/data/nvda-2026-10-27.json', help='dated real stock-price snapshot for the Action preview')\\n    26\\t    args = parser.parse_args()\\n    27\\t    if args.data:\\n    28\\t        data = json.loads(args.data.read_text())\\n    29\\t    else:\\n    30\\t        conn, items = service.open_ledger(str(args.ledger)), store.open_read_only(str(args.items))\\n    31\\t        try:\\n    32\\t            data = bundle.library(conn, items)\\n    33\\t        finally:\\n    34\\t            conn.close()\\n    35\\t            items.close()\\n    36\\t    if args.data and not data.get('schema_version') and args.ledger.exists():\\n    37\\t        conn = service.open_ledger(str(args.ledger))\\n    38\\t        try:\\n    39\\t            data['sequence_days'] = service.seq_day_map(conn)\\n    40\\t        finally:\\n    41\\t            conn.close()\\n    42\\t    ui = ROOT / 'poc/ui'\\n    43\\t    bundled = subprocess.run(['node', str(ui / 'build.mjs'), '--json'], capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    44\\t    if bundled.returncode:\\n    45\\t        print('UI build failed. Install its pinned dependencies with: npm ci --prefix poc/ui', file=sys.stderr)\\n    46\\t        print(bundled.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\\n    47\\t        bundled.check_returncode()\\n    48\\t    built = json.loads(bundled.stdout)\\n    49\\t    prepared = subprocess.run(['node', str(ui / 'prepare-data.mjs')], input=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False), capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    50\\t    if prepared.returncode:\\n    51\\t        print(prepared.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\\n    52\\t        prepared.check_returncode()\\n    53\\t    print(prepared.stderr.strip())\\n    54\\t    market = subprocess.run(['node', str(ui / 'prepare-data.mjs'), '--market'], input=args.market_data.read_text(), capture_output=True, text=True)\\n    55\\t    if market.returncode:\\n    56\\t        print(market.stderr, file=sys.stderr)\\n    57\\t        market.check_returncode()\\n    58\\t    print(market.stderr.strip())\\n    59\\t    template = (ROOT / 'poc/mock/index.template.html').read_text()\\n    60\\t    page = template.replace('__STYLES__', built['style']).replace('__SCRIPT__', built['script'].replace('</script', '<\\\\\\\\/script'))\\n    61\\t    page = page.replace('__DATA__', prepared.stdout.replace('<', '\\\\\\\\u003c'))\\n    62\\t    page = page.replace('__MARKET_DATA__', market.stdout.replace('<', '\\\\\\\\u003c'))\\n    63\\t    trials = json.loads(args.composite_trials.read_text()) if args.composite_trials else []\\n    64\\t    page = page.replace('__COMPOSITE_TRIALS__', json.dumps(trials, ensure_ascii=False).replace('<', '\\\\\\\\u003c'))\\n    65\\t    output = args.out.resolve()\\n    66\\t    output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    67\\t    temporary = output.with_suffix(output.suffix + '.tmp')\\n    68\\t    temporary.write_text(page)\\n    69\\t    temporary.replace(output)\\n    70\\t    print(f'UI: {len(built[\\\"script\\\"].encode()):,} JS bytes; wrote {output} ({len(page.encode()):,} bytes)')\\n    71\\t\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\tif __name__ == '__main__':\\n    74\\t    main()\\n     1\\timport { createThesisExplorer, createLibrary } from './index.js';\\n     2\\timport { fromBundles } from './adapters/bundle.js';\\n     3\\timport { parseDataset } from './model/contract.js';\\n     4\\timport { readIdea, readBundles, idsOf, graphOf, ideaCard } from './idea/idea.js';\\n     5\\timport { score, undirected } from './model/thesis.js';\\n     6\\timport { createIdeaDetail } from './idea/analysis.js';\\n     7\\timport {\\n     8\\t  prepareCompositeTrial,\\n     9\\t  prepareIdeaComposite,\\n    10\\t  compositeAt,\\n    11\\t  confidenceFromScore,\\n    12\\t  CompositeUnavailable,\\n    13\\t} from './idea/composite.js';\\n    14\\timport { DEFAULT_TRIGGER_CONDITION } from './model/trigger.js';\\n    15\\timport { advanceIdeaProgress } from './idea/progress.js';\\n    16\\timport { createIdeaComposer } from './components/idea-composer.js';\\n    17\\timport { DEFAULT_ACTION_SETTINGS } from './model/market.js';\\n    18\\texport * from './index.js';\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\tconst API = document.body.dataset.api || 'http://127.0.0.1:8788';\\n    21\\tconst input = document.getElementById('ask');\\n    22\\tconst root = document.getElementById('explorer');\\n    23\\tconst libraryRoot = document.getElementById('library');\\n    24\\tif (input && root && libraryRoot) {\\n    25\\t  try {\\n    26\\t    const initial = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('data').textContent);\\n    27\\t    let data = initial.schema_version ? parseDataset(initial) : fromBundles(initial);\\n    28\\t    const compositeTrials = JSON.parse(\\n    29\\t      document.getElementById('composite-trials')?.textContent || '[]',\\n    30\\t    );\\n    31\\t    // Explicit old exports remain usable for standalone component previews.\\n    32\\t    const library = createLibrary(libraryRoot, { dataset: data });\\n    33\\t    let app = null;\\n    34\\t    let inFlight = null;\\n    35\\t    let requestNumber = 0;\\n    36\\t    let deferredPresentation = null;\\n    37\\t    let leadingDirty = false;\\n    38\\t    const libraryRequest = new AbortController();\\n    39\\t    const form = document.getElementById('idea-form');\\n    40\\t    const send = document.getElementById('idea-send');\\n    41\\t    const composer = createIdeaComposer({\\n    42\\t      root,\\n    43\\t      form,\\n    44\\t      input,\\n    45\\t      launcher: document.getElementById('idea-launcher'),\\n    46\\t    });\\n    47\\t    const libraryButton = document.getElementById('show-library');\\n    48\\t    const ideaButton = document.getElementById('show-idea');\\n    49\\t    const idea = { text: '', state: 'idle', card: null, error: null };\\n    50\\t    let market = null;\\n    51\\t    try {\\n    52\\t      market = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('market-data')?.textContent || 'null');\\n    53\\t    } catch {\\n    54\\t      /* The card renders unavailable prices. */\\n    55\\t    }\\n    56\\t    const action = {\\n    57\\t      market,\\n    58\\t      settings: { ...DEFAULT_ACTION_SETTINGS },\\n    59\\t      onChange: (settings) => {\\n    60\\t        action.settings = settings;\\n    61\\t      },\\n    62\\t    };\\n    63\\t    const trigger = {\\n    64\\t      condition: { ...DEFAULT_TRIGGER_CONDITION },\\n    65\\t      getConfidence: () =>\\n    66\\t        idea.composite\\n    67\\t          ? confidenceFromScore(compositeAt(idea.composite, idea.day)?.value ?? null)\\n    68\\t          : null,\\n    69\\t      onChange: (condition) => {\\n    70\\t        trigger.condition = condition;\\n    71\\t      },\\n    72\\t    };\\n    73\\t    const ideaDetail = createIdeaDetail({ root: document.body });\\n    74\\t    function updateSendState() {\\n    75\\t      send.disabled = !input.value.trim() || Boolean(inFlight);\\n    76\\t      form.setAttribute('aria-busy', String(Boolean(inFlight)));\\n    77\\t    }\\n    78\\t    function cancelIdea() {\\n    79\\t      inFlight?.abort();\\n    80\\t      inFlight = null;\\n    81\\t      requestNumber++;\\n    82\\t      updateSendState();\\n    83\\t    }\\n    84\\t    function showLibrary() {\\n    85\\t      ideaDetail.close();\\n    86\\t      app?.pause();\\n    87\\t      root.hidden = true;\\n    88\\t      libraryRoot.hidden = false;\\n    89\\t      libraryButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\\n    90\\t      ideaButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');\\n    91\\t    }\\n    92\\t    function showIdea() {\\n    93\\t      library.close();\\n    94\\t      libraryRoot.hidden = true;\\n    95\\t      root.hidden = false;\\n    96\\t      libraryButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');\\n    97\\t      ideaButton.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\\n    98\\t      const firstVisit = !app;\\n    99\\t      if (firstVisit) {\\n   100\\t        app = createThesisExplorer(root, {\\n   101\\t          dataset: data,\\n   102\\t          onDayChange: (day, range) => {\\n   103\\t            idea.day = day;\\n   104\\t            idea.chartStart = range?.start;\\n   105\\t          },\\n   106\\t        });\\n   107\\t        app.showGraph({ day: library.getDay() });\\n   108\\t      }\\n   109\\t      if (deferredPresentation) {\\n   110\\t        const { spec, dataset } = deferredPresentation;\\n   111\\t        present(spec, dataset);\\n   112\\t      } else if (leadingDirty) {\\n   113\\t        app.updateLeading();\\n   114\\t        leadingDirty = false;\\n   115\\t      }\\n   116\\t      if (firstVisit) composer.open();\\n   117\\t      updateSendState();\\n   118\\t    }\\n   119\\t    function present(spec, dataset = null) {\\n   120\\t      if (root.hidden) {\\n   121\\t        deferredPresentation = { spec, dataset };\\n   122\\t        return;\\n   123\\t      }\\n   124\\t      if (dataset) app.setDataset(dataset);\\n   125\\t      app.showGraph({ ...spec, ...(idea.state === 'answered' ? { trigger, action } : {}) });\\n   126\\t      deferredPresentation = null;\\n   127\\t      leadingDirty = false;\\n   128\\t    }\\n   129\\t    const leadingCard = (layout = {}) =>\\n   130\\t      ideaCard({\\n     1\\timport fs from 'node:fs';\\n     2\\timport { performance } from 'node:perf_hooks';\\n     3\\timport { fromBundles } from './src/adapters/bundle.js';\\n     4\\timport { parseDataset } from './src/model/contract.js';\\n     5\\timport { readMarketSnapshot } from './src/model/market.js';\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\tconst source = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8'));\\n     8\\tconst start = performance.now();\\n     9\\tconst market = process.argv.includes('--market');\\n    10\\tconst dataset = market\\n    11\\t  ? readMarketSnapshot(source)\\n    12\\t  : source.schema_version\\n    13\\t    ? parseDataset(source)\\n    14\\t    : fromBundles(source);\\n    15\\tprocess.stderr.write(\\n    16\\t  `Validated ${market ? `${dataset.hourly.length + dataset.daily.length} price observations` : `${dataset.theses.length} theses`} in ${(performance.now() - start).toFixed(1)}ms\\\\n`,\\n    17\\t);\\n    18\\tprocess.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(dataset));\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:49:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_25\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,pathlib,collections,json,re,sys\\nsys.path.insert(0,'\\\\\\\\''src'\\\\\\\\'')\\nfrom hivemind import vocabulary,service\\ndef op(p):\\n c=sqlite3.connect(pathlib.Path(p).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\npaths=[('\\\\\\\\''old-'\\\\\\\\''+str(i),'\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-'\\\\\\\\''+str(i)+'\\\\\\\\''/prod'\\\\\\\\'') for i in (1,2,3)]+[('\\\\\\\\''sealed'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815'\\\\\\\\''),('\\\\\\\\''Xbox'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''poc/data/english-v23-jev-2026-10-25'\\\\\\\\'')]\\ndef loadviews(c):\\n keys=dict(c.execute('\\\\\\\\''select view_id,measure from view_keys'\\\\\\\\'')) if c.execute(\\\\\\\"select 1 from sqlite_master where name='\\\\\\\\''view_keys'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\").fetchone() else {}\\n views={}\\n for v,q in c.execute('\\\\\\\\''select view_id,question from views order by created_seq'\\\\\\\\''):\\n  rs=[dict(x) for x in c.execute('\\\\\\\\''select * from rungs where view_id=? order by position'\\\\\\\\'',(v,))]\\n  labels=tuple(vocabulary.canonical('\\\\\\\\''label'\\\\\\\\'',x['\\\\\\\\''label'\\\\\\\\'']) for x in rs)\\n  pair=sorted(labels)==['\\\\\\\\''No'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''Yes'\\\\\\\\'']\\n  event=keys.get(v) in ('\\\\\\\\''event'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''policy_event'\\\\\\\\'')\\n  views[v]=(q,labels,pair,event,rs)\\n return views\\nfor name,p in [paths[3],('\\\\\\\\''served'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828'\\\\\\\\'')]:\\n c=op(p+'\\\\\\\\''/views.sqlite'\\\\\\\\''); vs=loadviews(c); print(name,len(vs))\\n if name=='\\\\\\\\''served'\\\\\\\\'':\\n  print(collections.Counter((row[2],row[3]) for row in vs.values()))\\n  for vid,(q,l,pair,event,rs) in vs.items():\\n   if (event and not pair) or (not pair and not event and all(r.get('\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\'') is None and r.get('\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\'') is None for r in rs)):print(vid,q,l)\\n  continue\\n a=op('\\\\\\\\''poc/data/archive.sqlite'\\\\\\\\'')\\n for j in c.execute(\\\\\\\"select * from judgements\\\\\\\"):\\n  if not vs[j['\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\'']][2]: continue\\n  u=json.loads(a.execute('\\\\\\\\''select request_json from model_calls where call_id=? and request_sha256=?'\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\''])).fetchone()[0])['\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\''][-1]['\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\'']\\n  for block in u.split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\''):\\n   if block.startswith('\\\\\\\\''【它依赖的观点现在的结论'\\\\\\\\''): print([(x[:55],x[-15:]) for x in block.splitlines()[1:]])\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:50:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_25\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,pathlib,collections,json,re,sys\\nsys.path.insert(0,'\\\\\\\\''src'\\\\\\\\'')\\nfrom hivemind import vocabulary,service\\ndef op(p):\\n c=sqlite3.connect(pathlib.Path(p).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\npaths=[('\\\\\\\\''old-'\\\\\\\\''+str(i),'\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-'\\\\\\\\''+str(i)+'\\\\\\\\''/prod'\\\\\\\\'') for i in (1,2,3)]+[('\\\\\\\\''sealed'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815'\\\\\\\\''),('\\\\\\\\''Xbox'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''poc/data/english-v23-jev-2026-10-25'\\\\\\\\'')]\\ndef loadviews(c):\\n keys=dict(c.execute('\\\\\\\\''select view_id,measure from view_keys'\\\\\\\\'')) if c.execute(\\\\\\\"select 1 from sqlite_master where name='\\\\\\\\''view_keys'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\").fetchone() else {}\\n views={}\\n for v,q in c.execute('\\\\\\\\''select view_id,question from views order by created_seq'\\\\\\\\''):\\n  rs=[dict(x) for x in c.execute('\\\\\\\\''select * from rungs where view_id=? order by position'\\\\\\\\'',(v,))]\\n  labels=tuple(vocabulary.canonical('\\\\\\\\''label'\\\\\\\\'',x['\\\\\\\\''label'\\\\\\\\'']) for x in rs)\\n  pair=sorted(labels)==['\\\\\\\\''No'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''Yes'\\\\\\\\'']\\n  event=keys.get(v) in ('\\\\\\\\''event'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''policy_event'\\\\\\\\'')\\n  views[v]=(q,labels,pair,event,rs)\\n return views\\nfor name,p in [paths[3],('\\\\\\\\''served'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828'\\\\\\\\'')]:\\n c=op(p+'\\\\\\\\''/views.sqlite'\\\\\\\\''); vs=loadviews(c); print(name,len(vs))\\n if name=='\\\\\\\\''served'\\\\\\\\'':\\n  print(collections.Counter((row[2],row[3]) for row in vs.values()))\\n  for vid,(q,l,pair,event,rs) in vs.items():\\n   if (event and not pair) or (not pair and not event and all(r.get('\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\'') is None and r.get('\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\'') is None for r in rs)):print(vid,q,l)\\n  continue\\n a=op('\\\\\\\\''poc/data/archive.sqlite'\\\\\\\\'')\\n for j in c.execute(\\\\\\\"select * from judgements\\\\\\\"):\\n  if not vs[j['\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\'']][2]: continue\\n  u=json.loads(a.execute('\\\\\\\\''select request_json from model_calls where call_id=? and request_sha256=?'\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\''])).fetchone()[0])['\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\''][-1]['\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\'']\\n  for block in u.split('\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n'\\\\\\\\''):\\n   if block.startswith('\\\\\\\\''【它依赖的观点现在的结论'\\\\\\\\''): print([(x[:55],x[-15:]) for x in block.splitlines()[1:]])\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"sealed 94\\n[('- v14（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA与SK Group签署的综合合作能否在2026年12月31日前', '026-12-31仍不会落实。'), ('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', 'I工厂，不能证明出货开始时间。')]\\n[('- v14（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA与SK Group签署的综合合作能否在2026年12月31日前', '026-12-31仍不会落实。'), ('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '发生的事实证明量产出货已开始。')]\\n[('- v14（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA与SK Group签署的综合合作能否在2026年12月31日前', '026-12-31仍不会落实。'), ('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '能据此判定它们与目标时间矛盾。')]\\n[('- v14（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA与SK Group签署的综合合作能否在2026年12月31日前', '到来，这不是对届时结果的断言。'), ('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '能据此判定它们与目标时间矛盾。')]\\n[('- v14（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA与SK Group签署的综合合作能否在2026年12月31日前', '判断，不是对截止日结果的断言。'), ('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '，均不能证明量产出货已经发生。')]\\n[('- v14（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA与SK Group签署的综合合作能否在2026年12月31日前', '判断，不是对截止日结果的断言。'), ('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '，均不能证明量产出货已经发生。')]\\n[('- v14（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA与SK Group签署的综合合作能否在2026年12月31日前', '26-12-31最终仍未落实。'), ('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '026年下半年是否已开始出货。')]\\n[('- v54（开着；对方第一格是看多）Helios 生产爬坡能否使初始出货在2026年9月30日前开始？：现在 ', '，结论仍未被实际出货证据确认。')]\\n[('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '、e59、e61、e217）。')]\\n[('- v14（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA与SK Group签署的综合合作能否在2026年12月31日前', '断，并非对期限届满结果的确认。'), ('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '、e59、e61、e217）。')]\\n[('- v14（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA与SK Group签署的综合合作能否在2026年12月31日前', '26-12-31前的最终结果。'), ('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '217）也不等于此前不会出货。')]\\n[('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '217）也不等于此前不会出货。')]\\n[('- v7（开着；对方第一格是看多）NVIDIA能否在2026年下半年开始 Vera Rubin 量产出货？：现', '217）也不等于此前不会出货。')]\\nserved 68\\nCounter({(True, True): 54, (False, False): 13, (False, True): 1})\\nv49 Will the Commerce Department formally adopt a measure restricting Chinese AI developers’ access to Nvidia-powered computing capacity hosted outside China by 2027-01-31? ('Restriction adopted', 'No restriction adopted')\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72c.stream:51:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_26\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,pathlib,collections,json,re,sys\\nsys.path.insert(0,'\\\\\\\\''src'\\\\\\\\'')\\nfrom hivemind import vocabulary,service\\ndef op(p):\\n c=sqlite3.connect(pathlib.Path(p).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\n return c\\npaths=[('\\\\\\\\''old-'\\\\\\\\''+str(i),'\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-'\\\\\\\\''+str(i)+'\\\\\\\\''/prod'\\\\\\\\'') for i in (1,2,3)]+[('\\\\\\\\''sealed'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815'\\\\\\\\''),('\\\\\\\\''Xbox'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''poc/data/english-v23-jev-2026-10-25'\\\\\\\\'')]\\ndef loadviews(c):\\n keys=dict(c.execute('\\\\\\\\''select view_id,measure from view_keys'\\\\\\\\'')) if c.execute(\\\\\\\"select 1 from sqlite_master where name='\\\\\\\\''view_keys'\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\").fetchone() else {}\\n views={}\\n for v,q in c.execute('\\\\\\\\''select view_id,question from views order by created_seq'\\\\\\\\''):\\n  rs=[dict(x) for x in c.execute('\\\\\\\\''select * from rungs where view_id=? order by position'\\\\\\\\'',(v,))]\\n  labels=tuple(vocabulary.canonical('\\\\\\\\''label'\\\\\\\\'',x['\\\\\\\\''label'\\\\\\\\'']) for x in rs)\\n  pair=sorted(labels)==['\\\\\\\\''No'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''Yes'\\\\\\\\'']\\n  event=keys.get(v) in ('\\\\\\\\''event'\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\''policy_event'\\\\\\\\'')\\n  views[v]=(q,labels,pair,event,rs)\\n return views\\np='\\\\\\\\''poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828'\\\\\\\\''; c=op(p+'\\\\\\\\''/views.sqlite'\\\\\\\\'')\\nprint('\\\\\\\\''files'\\\\\\\\'',list(pathlib.Path(p).iterdir())[:20])\\nrows=c.execute(\\\\\\\"select judgement_id,publication_day,reasons,why_changed from judgements where view_id='\\\\\\\\''v49'\\\\\\\\'' order by judgement_id\\\\\\\").fetchall()\\nprint('\\\\\\\\''count'\\\\\\\\'',len(rows))\\nfor j in rows[:2]+rows[-2:]:print(dict(j))\\n'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n   110\t   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   111\t   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   112\t   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   113\t   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   114\t   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n   115\t3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   116\t   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n   117\t4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   118\t   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n   119\t\n   120\t## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n   121\t\n   122\t- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n   123\t  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n   124\t  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n   125\t- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n   126\t  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n   127\t  measured and reported apart.\n   128\t- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n   129\t- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n   130\t  counted after.\n   131\t- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n   132\t  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n   133\t  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n   134\t  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n   135\t    question\";\n   136\t  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n   137\t  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n   138\t  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n   139\t    or no question uses);\n   140\t  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n   141\t  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n   142\t    ones that matter one by one.\n   143\t- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n   144\t  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n   145\t  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n   146\t  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n   147\t    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n   148\t    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n   149\t      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n   150\t    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n   151\t      facts must not fall.\n   152\t  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n   153\t    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n   154\t      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n   155\t      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n   156\t      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n   157\t    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n   158\t      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n   159\t    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n   160\t      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n   161\t      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n   162\t      what was measured.\n   163\t  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n   164\t    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n   165\t  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n   166\t  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n   167\t\n   168\t## 7. Process (no drift)\n   169\t\n   170\t- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n   171\t  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n   172\t  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n   173\t- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n   174\t- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n   175\t  sentence, in both directions.\n   176\t- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n   177\t- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n   178\t\n   179\t## 8. Steps and where we are\n   180\t\n   181\t| # | Step | Output | Status |\n   182\t|---|---|---|---|\n   183\t| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n   184\t| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n   185\t| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n   186\t| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n   187\t| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n   188\t| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n   189\t| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n   190\t| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n   191\t| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n   192\t\n   193\t## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n   194\t\n   195\t- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n   196\t- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n   197\t- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n   198\t- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n   199\t- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n   200\t- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n   201\t- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
