{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.md | head -14 | cut -c1-1500; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74d.md | head -15 | cut -c1-1500'","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Not ready to build.** On macOS, an empty output folder created after the builder checks the path can be replaced by the final rename. A second problem is reproducible without touching a file: with a legacy ledger whose last judgement is September 20, the resolver accepts an explicit September 21 build, but revision 3 tells `check` to reject that package. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:98) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:126](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:126) · [service.py:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:64) · [Apple’s rename(2) manual](https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/System/Conceptual/ManPages_iPhoneOS/man2/rename.2.html)\n     2\t\n     3\t### 1. The 74b findings\n     4\t\n     5\t| Finding | Revision 3 |\n     6\t|---|---|\n     7\t| **1. Date, class, records and counts** | **Partly closed.** The builder passes its resolved date. The checker derives each class from the stored measure and labels, and compares lists with their multiplicities, so an added record fails. Two gaps remain. **Date:** `check` adds a ceiling that `build` does not apply, detailed below. **Order:** `created_seq` alone does not determine an ordered list. I verified that `old-2/v2` and `v3` both have sequence 8. The existing library breaks ties with `rowid`. Specify that same order for export and verification so two valid queries cannot disagree. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:77](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:77) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:98](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:98) · [bundle.py:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:232) |\n     8\t| **2. Missing source item** | **Behaviour closed. Test 13 is still insufficient.** The checker starts from every visible source row, takes its publication day there, and requires its item. But test 13 deletes only the item. A broken inner join would also refuse, because the finished package still contains the source the join dropped. For the decisive case, omit that source from a copy of the package as well, refresh its hash, and require refusal naming the missing item. The inner-join mutant would then accept it. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:114) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:287](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:287) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:305](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:305) |\n     9\t| **3. Regular files and unique JSON member names** | **Closed in the design.** `lstat` checks each of the two entries, and both files reject repeated names at every nesting level. For test 15 to prove the duplicate-name check, its altered data must have a matching manifest hash and a genuine value last in the repeated pair. Otherwise another check can refuse it even after duplicate detection is removed. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:129](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:129) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:291](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:291) |\n    10\t| **4. Staging ownership, errors and competing builds** | **Partly closed.** Exclusive, per-build staging resolves ownership. A competing builder’s finished, nonempty package survives. The empty-destination race and two error-handling gaps remain, detailed below. Test 9 also still requires an existing staging folder to block the build, contradicting the new crash-recovery rule. Test 14 should have both builds reach staging before either publishes, so a sequential retry cannot satisfy it. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:122](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:122) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:184](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:184) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:274) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:289](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:289) |\n    11\t| **5. Diagnostic columns** | **Closed.** The two optional judgement columns are read only where present, and the report records their absence. I verified that the served ledger has `reasons` and `why_changed` and lacks both `implied_outcome` and `reference`. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:339](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:339) |\n    12\t| **Builder-refusal test** | **Open.** Test 12 now reaches the right decision and names the right outcomes. Its in-process replacement of `release_export` violates AGENTS §4, which permits fakes only for external services. The scratch-copy test below exercises the real command. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:281](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:281) · [AGENTS.md:151](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:151) |\n    13\t\n    14\t### 2. The evidence-summary disagreement\n     1\t**Not ready to build.** Revision 4 closes most of 74c. Two issues remain serious enough to block the build design. Publication or cleanup can remove another owner’s empty folder, and an ordinary database error can leave an empty output folder that blocks the next build.\n     2\t\n     3\t### 1. The 74c findings\n     4\t\n     5\t| Finding | Verdict |\n     6\t|---|---|\n     7\t| One date rule | **Closed.** Both commands use `resolve_bound`. An explicit date on a legacy ledger can pass both commands, and a date after a recorded completed day is refused. For test 10, choose a legacy date later than its last judgement so the fixture distinguishes revision 4 from revision 3. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:107](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:107) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:306](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:306) · [service.py:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:64) |\n     8\t| `created_seq, rowid` order | **Closed.** Export and verification specify the same tie-breaker the existing library uses. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:88) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:115) · [bundle.py:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:232) |\n     9\t| Move preserves a folder the build did not create | **Open.** `mkdir` establishes who created the directory at that instant. The later `rename` replaces whichever empty directory occupies that name when it runs. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:133](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:133) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:142) |\n    10\t| Cleanup where the staging path is known | **Closed for the reported write failure.** `write_package` removes staging if either write fails before it returns the path. After it returns, the caller knows the path. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:137](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:137) |\n    11\t| Outcome after publication | **Closed.** A report-write failure leaves the checked package in place, returns exit 2, and directs the user to `check`. The regenerated report marks the original export time as unmeasured. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:169](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:169) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173) |\n    12\t| Test 12 through the real command | **Closed.** The unchanged command succeeds. The writer fault then gives the specific refusal and leaves no output or staging folder. Removing only the staged check lets the bad package reach the destination. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:309](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:309) |\n    13\t| Tests 9, 13, 14 and 15 | **9, 13 and 15 closed.** Test 9 permits unrelated staging. Test 13 removes the matching source and refreshes the hash, so a checker that silently drops a missing item would accept the pair. Test 15 puts the genuine value last and refreshes the hash, isolating duplicate-name detection. **14 partly closed.** It overlaps two builds, but its empty-folder case occurs before the claim. Its later case uses a nonempty folder. Neither exercises a different *empty* folder at publication. Also, direct calls to module functions cannot establish the command’s claimed exit status. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:301](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:301) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:315](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:315) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:318](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:318) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:324](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:324) |\n    14\t\n    15\t### 2. What must change before building\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
