{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '191,261p'; nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '91,122p;418,430p'\"","aggregated_output":"   191\t  - counts per class;\n   192\t  - the unresolved list;\n   193\t  - the fields compared;\n   194\t  - bytes;\n   195\t  - `export_seconds` (build only) and `check_seconds`.\n   196\t\n   197\t## 2. State × event (one export, read-only)\n   198\t\n   199\t| State / event | What happens | What is written | Day used |\n   200\t|---|---|---|---|\n   201\t| Store's first day still in progress | `FirstDayNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | none |\n   202\t| Store with no completed day and no judgement, `--as-of` omitted | refused: \"no default day; supply --as-of\" | nothing | none |\n   203\t| `--as-of` not a valid date (`2026-08-99`) | refused by `date.fromisoformat` | nothing | none |\n   204\t| `--as-of` after the last completed day | `BoundNotCompleted`; the build stops | nothing | requested day |\n   205\t| `--as-of` valid, before the first visible question | empty `questions`; the report says 0 | package | bound |\n   206\t| `--as-of` omitted | last completed day (a legacy ledger: its last judgement day) | package | resolved bound |\n   207\t| View created after the bound | not exported | — | bound |\n   208\t| View closed on or before the bound | `open: false`, with no reason and no day | — | bound |\n   209\t| Closed, then reopened, before the bound | the last visible switch wins | — | bound |\n   210\t| Event or Yes/No not yet judged at the bound | `answer: null` | — | bound |\n   211\t| Evidence replaced on or before the bound | excluded; the replacement is in force | — | bound |\n   212\t| Evidence replaced after the bound | kept | — | bound |\n   213\t| Source recorded after the bound | excluded | — | bound |\n   214\t| Visible source with no row in the items database | `ReleaseRefused`, naming the evidence and input id | nothing final | bound |\n   215\t| Store written by a live run | not supported. The builder is given a snapshot (AGENTS §9), and both connections are pinned | — | — |\n   216\t| `--out` exists, empty or not, at the start | refused early; `publish` would also refuse | nothing | — |\n   217\t| `check_export`, `check_package` or `check_origins` refuses | this build's staging folder is removed, exit non-zero | nothing final | — |\n   218\t| A write, check or move fails, or a database error (`sqlite3.Error`, such as an items database with no `items` table) | exit 1; the `finally` removes this build's staging; a corrected retry at the same `--out` succeeds | nothing | — |\n   219\t| A folder, empty or not, appears at `--out` after staging | `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`; that folder is untouched; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing of this build | — |\n   220\t| The filesystem has no atomic no-replace move | `publish` refuses; staging removed; exit 1 | nothing | — |\n   221\t| Crash while staging | a uniquely named staging folder is left as debris. Nothing is at `--out`, and no later build is blocked | staging only | — |\n   222\t| Crash after the rename, before the report | the package is final and checked; `check` rewrites the report | package | — |\n   223\t| The report write fails after publication | exit 2: the package is final and checked; `check` regenerates the report | package | — |\n   224\t| Two builds aimed at one `--out` | each stages privately; the first `publish` wins; the second's `publish` refuses with `EEXIST`, and its `finally` removes only its own staging | the winner's package | — |\n   225\t| Package `as_of` later than the store's last completed day (`check`) | refused by `resolve_bound` | nothing | package `as_of` |\n   226\t| A legacy ledger with no completed days, explicit day | the build and `check` both accept any valid date (one rule) | package | requested day |\n   227\t| A package file is a symbolic link, or a JSON member name repeats | `check_package` refuses | nothing | — |\n   228\t| The package's `class` disagrees with the store's (a Yes/No answer replaced by the marker) | `check_origins` refuses: class is derived from the store | nothing final | bound |\n   229\t| Store or configuration changed between builds | each package records its bound and data sha256; the report names the store path | — | — |\n   230\t| Legacy ledger: no `view_keys` table, `是`/`否` labels | no key, so no event; the labels canonicalise to Yes/No | — | — |\n   231\t\n   232\t## 3. Value × reader\n   233\t\n   234\tReaders of the package:\n   235\t- `check_package` and `check_origins`;\n   236\t- the release page (slice 2);\n   237\t- the tests.\n   238\t\n   239\tThe report's reader is the person building. No POC code imports `release`.\n   240\t\n   241\t| Value | Permitted source at the bound | Checked by |\n   242\t|---|---|---|\n   243\t| `id`, `question` | `views.view_id`, `views.question` | `check_origins` |\n   244\t| `open` | the latest visible `view_switches.open` | `check_origins` |\n   245\t| `class` | `view_keys.measure`, `rungs.label` | `check_origins` derives it from the store; tests and mutants check the identity rule |\n   246\t| `answers`, `answer` | `rungs.label` by position; the latest `judgements.rung` on or before the bound | `check_origins` |\n   247\t| `forecast` | the constant marker | `check_export` |\n   248\t| evidence fields | the `evidence` row; visible `evidence_links` minus visible replacements | `check_origins` |\n   249\t| source fields | every visible `evidence_sources` row (`publication_day` as `day`); its `items` row's `title`, `publisher`, `source_uri`, required | `check_origins` (left join; a missing item refuses) |\n   250\t| manifest | the data's `format`, `allow_list`, `as_of`; the data sha256 | `check_package` |\n   251\t| report (outside the package) | `ladder_bands` per number question; counts | read by the builder's user |\n   252\t\n   253\t**Never read by `release_export`:**\n   254\t- `rungs.condition`, `lo`, `hi`;\n   255\t- `judgements.reasons`, `why_changed`, `implied_outcome`, `reference`, `pushes_json`, `theme_pushes_json`, `cited_*`;\n   256\t- `view_switches.reason`;\n   257\t- `clean_ladders`;\n   258\t- `thesis_groups`;\n   259\t- `dependencies`, `successions`.\n   260\t\n   261\t## 4. New path × old checks\n    91\t## 2. Before writing code: design\n    92\t\n    93\tCode written before the thinking costs rounds of review. A design holds these tables before code and before any review; a blank cell\n    94\tmeans it is not ready:\n    95\t\n    96\t1. **State × event**, for work that spans more than one step, run or day: every state against every event it can meet (success,\n    97\t   refusal, a refused retry, an external failure, a crash midway, work still in flight when a run ends, a later run on a later date,\n    98\t   configuration changed in between, an input corrected while waiting, another writer of the same data, two scopes at once), including\n    99\t   the work before its first step and after its terminal outcome. Each cell names the transition, what is written, and the date every\n   100\t   read and write uses.\n   101\t2. **Value × reader.** Every value a change writes, against every reader of it (found by searching the field) and every input source the\n   102\t   value can come from. A rule over a kind of data lists every writer of that kind. A change to how often something fires is counted\n   103\t   against every reader of its output.\n   104\t3. **New path × old checks.** For a new input, derived value, mode or changed data shape: every check the old path passes, and whether\n   105\t   the new one meets it. A changed shape re-derives every check written for the old one.\n   106\t4. **Prior decisions.** The decisions searched for the mechanism by name; any decision that rejected or bounded it is quoted in the\n   107\t   design and in the question to Alex.\n   108\t\n   109\t- A contract over text or shapes states the closed set of what passes (a full match); anything else fails or is not judged. Enumerate\n   110\t  the accepted set against every context and reader it meets before the first edit.\n   111\t- **Code owns identity, never importance.** Before building a closed list, enum or gate, write which decision it takes from the model\n   112\t  and whether that decision is identity (\"are these the same thing?\") or judgement (\"does this matter?\"); build only the identity part.\n   113\t  A list of what matters is at most a hint shown to the model (Alex, 2026-10-25: \"你这个做法难道不是非常的限死吗？永远都是一堆财务指标，真正的观点呢？\").\n   114\t- **No case-fitted fix.** A hand list, a special path or a rule fitted to the case in view fixes that case and breaks the next. First ask\n   115\t  whether the judge had the material and the definition it needed, and whether a typed field is missing; run the proposal against the\n   116\t  existing tests and the gold for a counter-example before building (D167: \"我不要 hardcode 解法 it's premature optimization, not general root fix\").\n   117\t- A blind review measures the tables. A serious finding they do not hold shows a missing dimension: add it and walk every row again,\n   118\t  never answer the finding alone. Code starts when the review finds nothing serious. A design whose core contract is still open is a\n   119\t  question, not something to build.\n   120\t- A foundation's acceptance carries a size and speed budget from its first control, not only correctness.\n   121\t\n   122\t## 3. Writing code\n   418\t\n   419\t## 9. Workspace and operations\n   420\t\n   421\t- Inspect a path before writing to it; new stored data gets a new, dated name; chain guarded steps with `&&`. Deleting stored data needs\n   422\t  Alex's request, a backup, exactly identified items and a log entry.\n   423\t- Absolute paths. Commands run under zsh: pass a list as an array. No foreground `sleep`.\n   424\t- Preserve existing and concurrent changes: never reset, clean or stash work that is not yours. Never run parallel agents that edit\n   425\t  shared modules.\n   426\t- When Alex names a step, the test is that step alone through its own harness (extraction: stored requests re-sent, answers sifted,\n   427\t  scored against the gold). A full-pipeline run, a registered test, or a paid send beyond the probes of a few cents an agreed direction\n   428\t  allows (§7.3) starts only on his explicit word (Alex, 2026-10-27: \"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\").\n   429\t- A long paid run is launched detached in a new session with a log and pid file, after checking machine and network health; nothing heavy\n   430\t  runs beside paid calls. A gate runs on a snapshot no one is editing.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src python3.13 -B -c 'import sqlite3; from pathlib import Path; from hivemind import service; from datetime import date; p=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\\\"); src=sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True); db=sqlite3.connect(\\\":memory:\\\"); src.backup(db); db.row_factory=sqlite3.Row; print([tuple(r) for r in db.execute(\\\"pragma table_info(days_completed)\\\")]); print(tuple(db.execute(\\\"select * from days_completed order by id desc limit 1\\\").fetchone()))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
