{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready to build.** Revision 6 closes both 74e findings. Two other issues remain. A package dated August 25 can include September evidence, and writing the report can overwrite an input database.\n\n**1. Both 74e findings are closed in the design.**\n\n- **Late refusal.** Test 14 now pauses the real command immediately before `publish`, creates an empty `--out`, and resumes. It requires exit 1, removal of this build’s staging folder, and survival of the same empty directory, verified by device and inode. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:336](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:336)\n- **Cleanup after publication.** The builder clears its staging path immediately after the move succeeds. Test 14 recreates the freed name with a marker file and requires the marker to survive command exit. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:173) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:339](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:339)\n\n**2. Two findings block the build.**\n\n- **The date must be normalized before comparison.** Python accepts `20260825` and `2026-08-25` as the same day. The design passes the original text to `resolve_bound`, and evidence visibility also compares dates as text. I reproduced the consequence on an in-memory copy of `old-1`, adding only a completed day in January 2027. For `v8`, `2026-08-25` returned 621 evidence records through August 25. `20260825` returned 1,284 through September 20. Parse an explicit date before calling `resolve_bound`, use its `YYYY-MM-DD` form for every query, and require that form in the package. Test that both command-line spellings produce the same evidence. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:95) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:121](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:121) · [service.py:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:69) · [service.py:113](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:113)\n- **The report can replace the ledger or items database.** For example, with `--out /work/release` and a valid SQLite input named `/work/release.report.json`, the build can read the input, verify and publish the package, then replace that database with JSON. The standalone `check` command rewrites the same path. Both commands should refuse a report destination that resolves to either input before writing anything. The decisive test is that each command refuses the collision and the input’s bytes remain intact. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:166](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:166) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:175) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:185](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:185)"}}
